ess from the second column of the Data Range list box. You can change the range in the text box or by dragging in the document. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the Select data range button.␀tp_DataSource|extended_tip|IMB_RANGE_CATShows the source range address of the categories (the texts you can see on the x-axis of a category chart). For an XY-chart, the text box contains the source range of the data labels which are displayed for the data points. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the Select data range button.␀tp_DataSource|extended_tip|IMB_RANGE_MAINShows the source range address from the second column of the Data Range list box. You can change the range in the text box or by dragging in the document. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the Select data range button.␀tp_DataSource|extended_tip|LB_ROLEShows all the data ranges used by the data series that is selected in the Data Series list box. Each data range shows the role name and the source range address.␀tp_DataSource|extended_tip|LB_SERIESShows a list of all data series in the chart. Click an entry to view and edit that data series. Click Add to insert a new series into the list after the selected entry.␀tp_DataSource|imageIMB_RANGE_CAT|tooltip_textSelect data range␀tp_DataSource|imageIMB_RANGE_MAIN|tooltip_textSelect data range␀tp_DataTable|horizontalBorderCBShow horizontal border␀tp_DataTable|keysCBShow keys␀tp_DataTable|outlineCBShow outline␀tp_DataTable|verticalBorderCBShow vertical border␀tp_ErrorBars|CB_SYN_POS_NEGSame value for both␀tp_ErrorBars|FT_NEGATIVE_Negative (-)␀tp_ErrorBars|FT_POSITIVEP_ositive (+)␀tp_ErrorBars|IB_RANGE_NEGATIVE|tooltip_textSelect data range␀tp_ErrorBars|IB_RANGE_POSITIVE|tooltip_textSelect data range␀tp_ErrorBars|RB_BOTHPositive _and Negative␀tp_ErrorBars|RB_CONST_Constant Value␀tp_ErrorBars|RB_NEGATIVENe_gative␀tp_ErrorBars|RB_NONE_None␀tp_ErrorBars|RB_PERCENT_Percentage␀tp_ErrorBars|RB_POSITIVEPos_itive␀tp_ErrorBars|RB_RANGECell _Range␀tp_ErrorBars|STR_CONTROLTEXT_ERROR_BARS_FROM_DATAFrom Data Table␀tp_ErrorBars|STR_DATA_SELECT_RANGE_FOR_NEGATIVE_ERRORBARSSelect Range for Negative Error Bars␀tp_ErrorBars|STR_DATA_SELECT_RANGE_FOR_POSITIVE_ERRORBARSSelect Range for Positive Error Bars␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|CB_SYN_POS_NEGEnable to use the positive error values also as negative error values. You can only change the value of the "Positive (+)" box. That value gets copied to the "Negative (-)" box automatically.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|ED_RANGE_NEGATIVEEnter the address range from where to get the negative error values. Use the Shrink button to select the range from a sheet.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|ED_RANGE_POSITIVEEnter the address range from where to get the positive error values. Use the Shrink button to select the range from a sheet.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|IB_RANGE_NEGATIVEClick a button to shrink the dialog, then use the mouse to select the cell range in the spreadsheet. Click the button again to restore the dialog to full size.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|IB_RANGE_POSITIVEClick a button to shrink the dialog, then use the mouse to select the cell range in the spreadsheet. Click the button again to restore the dialog to full size.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|LB_FUNCTIONSelect a function to calculate the error bars.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|MF_NEGATIVEEnter the value to subtract from the displayed value as the negative error value.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|MF_POSITIVEEnter the value to add to the displayed value as the positive error value.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|RB_BOTHShows positive and negative error bars.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|RB_CONSTDisplays constant values that you specify in the Parameters area.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|RB_FUNCTIONSelect a function to calculate the error bars.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|RB_NEGATIVEShows only negative error bars.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|RB_NONEDoes not show any error bars.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|RB_PERCENTDisplays a percentage. The display refers to the corresponding data point. Set the percentage in the Parameters area.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|RB_POSITIVEShows only positive error bars.␀tp_ErrorBars|extended_tip|RB_RANGEClick Cell Range and then specify a cell range from which to take the positive and negative error bar values.␀tp_ErrorBars|label1Error Category␀tp_ErrorBars|label2Error Indicator␀tp_ErrorBars|label3Parameters␀tp_ErrorBars|liststoreFUNCTIONError Margin␀tp_ErrorBars|liststoreFUNCTIONStandard Deviation␀tp_ErrorBars|liststoreFUNCTIONStandard Error␀tp_ErrorBars|liststoreFUNCTIONVariance␀tp_LegendPosition|CB_NO_OVERLAYShow the legend without overlapping the chart␀tp_LegendPosition|FT_LEGEND_TEXTDIRTe_xt direction␀tp_LegendPosition|TXT_ORIENTATIONText Orientation␀tp_LegendPosition|TXT_OVERLAYOverlay␀tp_LegendPosition|TXT_POSITIONPosition␀tp_LegendPosition|bottom_Bottom␀tp_LegendPosition|extended_tip|CB_NO_OVERLAYSpecifies whether the legend should overlap the chart.␀tp_LegendPosition|extended_tip|LB_LEGEND_TEXTDIRSpecify the text direction for a paragraph that uses complex text layout (CTL). This feature is only available if complex text layout support is enabled.␀tp_LegendPosition|extended_tip|bottomPositions the legend at the bottom of the chart.␀tp_LegendPosition|extended_tip|leftPositions the legend at the left of the chart.␀tp_LegendPosition|extended_tip|rightPositions the legend at the right of the chart.␀tp_LegendPosition|extended_tip|topPositions the legend at the top of the chart.␀tp_LegendPosition|left_Left␀tp_LegendPosition|right_Right␀tp_LegendPosition|top_Top␀tp_PolarOptions|CB_CLOCKWISE_Clockwise direction␀tp_PolarOptions|CB_INCLUDE_HIDDEN_CELLS_POLARInclude _values from hidden cells␀tp_PolarOptions|FT_ROTATION_DEGREES_Degrees␀tp_PolarOptions|extended_tip|CB_CLOCKWISEThe default direction in which the pieces of a pie chart are ordered is counterclockwise. Enable the Clockwise direction checkbox to draw the pieces in opposite direction.␀tp_PolarOptions|extended_tip|CT_ANGLE_DIALDrag the small dot along the circle or click any position on the circle to set the starting angle of a pie or donut chart. The starting angle is the mathematical angle position where the first piece is drawn. The value of 90 degrees draws the first piece at the 12 o'clock position. A value of 0 degrees starts at the 3 o'clock position.␀tp_PolarOptions|extended_tip|NF_STARTING_ANGLEEnter the starting angle between 0 and 359 degrees. You can also click the arrows to change the displayed value.␀tp_PolarOptions|label1Orientation␀tp_PolarOptions|label2Starting Angle␀tp_PolarOptions|label3Plot Options␀tp_RangeChooser|CB_FIRST_COLUMN_ASLABELSF_irst column as label␀tp_RangeChooser|CB_FIRST_ROW_ASLABELS_First row as label␀tp_RangeChooser|CB_TIME_BASEDTime based charting␀tp_RangeChooser|FT_CAPTION_FOR_WIZARDChoose a Data Range␀tp_RangeChooser|FT_RANGE_Data range:␀tp_RangeChooser|IB_RANGE|tooltip_textSelect data range␀tp_RangeChooser|RB_DATACOLSData series in _columns␀tp_RangeChooser|RB_DATAROWSData series in _rows␀tp_RangeChooser|STR_PAGE_DATA_RANGEData Range␀tp_RangeChooser|extended_tip|CB_FIRST_COLUMN_ASLABELSFor data series in columns: The first column in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first column in the range is used as categories. The remaining columns comprise the data columns. If this check box is not selected, all columns are data columns.␀tp_RangeChooser|extended_tip|CB_FIRST_ROW_ASLABELSFor data series in columns: The first row in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first row in the range is used as categories. The remaining rows comprise the data series. If this check box is not selected, all rows are data series.␀tp_RangeChooser|extended_tip|ED_RANGEEnter the data range that you want to include in your chart. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the Select data range button.␀tp_RangeChooser|extended_tip|IB_RANGEEnter the data range that you want to include in your chart. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the Select data range button.␀tp_RangeChooser|extended_tip|RB_DATACOLSData series get their data from consecutive columns in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data column will contain x-values for all series. All other data columns are used as y-values, one for each series.␀tp_RangeChooser|extended_tip|RB_DATAROWSData series get their data from consecutive rows in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data series will contain x-values for all series. All other data series are used as y-values, one for each series.␀tp_RangeChooser|imageIB_RANGE|tooltip_textSelect data range␀tp_RangeChooser|label1Start Table Index␀tp_RangeChooser|label2End Table Index␀tp_Scale|CBX_AUTO_MAXA_utomatic␀tp_Scale|CBX_AUTO_MIN_Automatic␀tp_Scale|CBX_AUTO_ORIGINAutomat_ic␀tp_Scale|CBX_AUTO_STEP_HELPAut_omatic␀tp_Scale|CBX_AUTO_STEP_MAINAu_tomatic␀tp_Scale|CBX_AUTO_TIME_RESOLUTIONAutomat_ic␀tp_Scale|CBX_LOGARITHM_Logarithmic scale␀tp_Scale|CBX_REVERSE_Reverse direction␀tp_Scale|DATE-RESOLUTIONDays␀tp_Scale|DATE-RESOLUTIONMonths␀tp_Scale|DATE-RESOLUTIONYears␀tp_Scale|FL_SCALEScale␀tp_Scale|LB_AXIS_TYPEAutomatic␀tp_Scale|LB_AXIS_TYPEDate␀tp_Scale|LB_AXIS_TYPEText␀tp_Scale|TXT_AXIS_TYPET_ype␀tp_Scale|TXT_MAXMa_ximum␀tp_Scale|TXT_MIN_Minimum␀tp_Scale|TXT_ORIGINRe_ference value␀tp_Scale|TXT_STEP_HELPMinor inter_val␀tp_Scale|TXT_STEP_HELP_COUNTMinor inter_val count␀tp_Scale|TXT_STEP_MAINMa_jor interval␀tp_Scale|TXT_TIME_RESOLUTIONR_esolution␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|CBX_AUTO_ORIGINYou must first deselect the Automatic option in order to modify the values.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|CBX_LOGARITHMSpecifies that you want the axis to be subdivided logarithmically.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|CBX_REVERSEDefines where the lower and where the higher values are displayed at the axis. The unchecked state is the mathematical direction.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|EDT_MAXDefines the maximum value for the end of the axis.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|EDT_MINDefines the minimum value for the beginning of the axis.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|EDT_ORIGINSpecifies at which position to display the values along the axis.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|EDT_STEP_MAINDefines the interval for the main division of the axes.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|LB_AXIS_TYPEFor some types of axes, you can select to format an axis as text or date, or to detect the type automatically.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|LB_HELP_TIME_UNITMinor interval can be set to show a certain number of days, months, or years.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|LB_MAIN_TIME_UNITMajor interval can be set to show a certain number of days, months, or years.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|LB_TIME_RESOLUTIONResolution can be set to show days, months, or years as interval steps.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|MT_MAIN_DATE_STEPMajor interval can be set to show a certain number of days, months, or years.␀tp_Scale|extended_tip|MT_STEPHELPDefines the interval for the subdivision of the axes.␀tp_Scale|liststoreDATEDays␀tp_Scale|liststoreDATEMonths␀tp_Scale|liststoreDATEYears␀tp_SeriesToAxis|CB_BARS_SIDE_BY_SIDEShow _bars side by side␀tp_SeriesToAxis|CB_CONNECTORConnection lines␀tp_SeriesToAxis|CB_INCLUDE_HIDDEN_CELLSInclude _values from hidden cells␀tp_SeriesToAxis|CB_LEGEND_ENTRY_HIDDENHide legend entry␀tp_SeriesToAxis|FT_GAP_Spacing␀tp_SeriesToAxis|FT_MISSING_VALUESPlot missing values␀tp_SeriesToAxis|FT_OVERLAP_Overlap␀tp_SeriesToAxis|RBT_OPT_AXIS_1Primary Y axis␀tp_SeriesToAxis|RBT_OPT_AXIS_2Secondary Y axis␀tp_SeriesToAxis|RB_ASSUME_ZERO_Assume zero␀tp_SeriesToAxis|RB_CONTINUE_LINE_Continue line␀tp_SeriesToAxis|RB_DONT_PAINT_Leave gap␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|CB_BARS_SIDE_BY_SIDEThe bars from different data series are shown as if they were attached only to one axis.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|CB_CONNECTORFor "stacked" and "percent" column (vertical bar) charts, mark this check box to connect the column layers that belong together with lines.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|CB_INCLUDE_HIDDEN_CELLSCheck to also show values of currently hidden cells within the source cell range.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|CB_LEGEND_ENTRY_HIDDENDo not show legend entry for the selected data series or data point.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|MT_GAPDefines the spacing between the columns in percent.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|MT_OVERLAPDefines the necessary settings for overlapping data series.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|RBT_OPT_AXIS_1This option is active as default. All data series are aligned to the primary Y axis.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|RBT_OPT_AXIS_2Changes the scaling of the Y axis. This axis is only visible when at least one data series is assigned to it and the axis view is active.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|RB_ASSUME_ZEROFor a missing value, the y-value will be shown as zero. This is the default for chart type Area.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|RB_CONTINUE_LINEFor a missing value, the interpolation from the neighbor values will be shown. This is the default for chart type XY.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|extended_tip|RB_DONT_PAINTFor a missing value, no data will be shown. This is the default for chart types Column, Bar, Line, Net.␀tp_SeriesToAxis|label1Align Data Series to␀tp_SeriesToAxis|label2Settings␀tp_SeriesToAxis|label3Plot Options␀tp_SeriesToAxis|label4Legend Entry␀tp_Trendline|exponential_Exponential␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|degreeDegree of polynomial trend line.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|entry_XnameName of X variable in trend line equation.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|entry_YnameName of Y variable in trend line equation.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|entry_nameName of trend line in legend.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|exponentialAn exponential trend line is shown.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|interceptValueValue of intercept if it is forced.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|label10How the trend line is calculated.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|label3Degree of polynomial trend line.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|label4Number of points to calculate average of moving average trend line.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|label5Name of trend line in legend.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|label6Name of X variable in trend line equation.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|label7Trend line is extrapolated for higher x-values.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|label8Trend line is extrapolated for lower x-values.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|label9Name of Y variable in trend line equation.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|linearA linear trend line is shown.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|logarithmicA logarithmic trend line is shown.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|movingAverageA moving average trend line is shown with a given period.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|periodNumber of points to calculate average of moving average trend line.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|polynomialA polynomial trend line is shown with a given degree.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|powerA power trend line is shown.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|setInterceptFor linear, polynomial and exponential trend lines, intercept value is forced to a given value.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|showCorrelationCoefficientShows the coefficient of determination next to the trend line.␀tp_Trendline|extended_tip|showEquationShows the trend line equation next to the trend line.␀tp_Trendline|label1Regression Type␀tp_Trendline|label10_Type␀tp_Trendline|label2Options␀tp_Trendline|label3Degree␀tp_Trendline|label4Period␀tp_Trendline|label5Trendline _Name␀tp_Trendline|label6_X Variable Name␀tp_Trendline|label7Extrapolate Forward␀tp_Trendline|label8Extrapolate Backward␀tp_Trendline|label9_Y Variable Name␀tp_Trendline|linear_Linear␀tp_Trendline|liststore_moving_typeAveraged Abscissa␀tp_Trendline|liststore_moving_typeCentral␀tp_Trendline|liststore_moving_typePrior␀tp_Trendline|logarithmicL_ogarithmic␀tp_Trendline|movingAverage_Moving Average␀tp_Trendline|polynomial_Polynomial␀tp_Trendline|powerPo_wer␀tp_Trendline|setInterceptForce _Intercept␀tp_Trendline|showCorrelationCoefficientShow _Coefficient of Determination (R²)␀tp_Trendline|showEquationShow E_quation␀tp_axisLabel|autoA_utomatic␀tp_axisLabel|breakCB_Break␀tp_axisLabel|degreeL_Degrees␀tp_axisLabel|evenStagger _even␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|OrientDegreeAllows you to manually enter the orientation angle.␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|autoAutomatically arranges numbers on the axis.␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|breakCBAllows a text break.␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|dialCtrlClicking anywhere on the wheel defines the variable text orientation.␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|evenStagger numbers on the axis, odd numbers lower than even numbers.␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|oddStaggers numbers on the axis, even numbers lower than odd numbers.␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|overlapCBSpecifies that the text in cells may overlap other cells.␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|showlabelsCBSpecifies whether to show or hide the axis labels.␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|stackedCBAssigns vertical text orientation for cell contents.␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|textdirLBSpecify the text direction for a paragraph that uses complex text layout (CTL). This feature is only available if complex text layout support is enabled.␀tp_axisLabel|extended_tip|tileArranges numbers on the axis side by side.␀tp_axisLabel|labelABCDABCD␀tp_axisLabel|labelTextOrientText Orientation␀tp_axisLabel|oddSt_agger odd␀tp_axisLabel|orderLOrder␀tp_axisLabel|overlapCBO_verlap␀tp_axisLabel|showlabelsCBSho_w labels␀tp_axisLabel|stackedCBVe_rtically stacked␀tp_axisLabel|textdirLTe_xt direction:␀tp_axisLabel|textflowLData Table Properties␀tp_axisLabel|textflowLText Flow␀tp_axisLabel|tile_Tile␀wizelementspage|AxeChoose Titles, Legend, and Grid Settings␀wizelementspage|bottom_Bottom␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|bottomPositions the legend at the bottom of the chart.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|leftPositions the legend at the left of the chart.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|maintitleEnter a title for your chart.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|primaryXaxisEnter a label for the x-axis (horizontal).␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|primaryYaxisEnter a label for the y-axis (vertical).␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|primaryZaxisEnter a label for the z-axis. This option is only available for three-dimensional charts.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|rightPositions the legend at the right of the chart.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|secondaryXaxisEnter a label for the secondary x-axis. This option is only available for charts that support a secondary x-axis.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|showSpecifies whether to display a legend for the chart.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|subtitleEnter a subtitle for your chart.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|topPositions the legend at the top of the chart.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|xDisplays grid lines that are perpendicular to the x-axis.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|yDisplays grid lines that are perpendicular to the y-axis.␀wizelementspage|extended_tip|zDisplays grid lines that are perpendicular to the z-axis. This option is only available for three-dimensional charts.␀wizelementspage|label2Display Grids␀wizelementspage|labelMainTitle_Title␀wizelementspage|labelPrimaryXaxis_X axis␀wizelementspage|labelPrimaryYaxis_Y axis␀wizelementspage|labelPrimaryZaxis_Z axis␀wizelementspage|labelSecondaryXAxisX _axis␀wizelementspage|labelSecondaryYAxisY ax_is␀wizelementspage|labelSubTitle_Subtitle␀wizelementspage|left_Left␀wizelementspage|right_Right␀wizelementspage|show_Display legend␀wizelementspage|top_Top␀wizelementspage|xX axis␀wizelementspage|yY ax_is␀wizelementspage|zZ axi_s␀Project-Id-Version: PACKAGE VERSION
