␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;␀␀␀EditDictionaryDialogIn the Edit Custom Dictionary dialog you have the option to enter new terms or edit existing entries.␀FileExtCheckDialog|Ok_Button_OK␀FileExtCheck|Checkbox_Perform check on startup␀FileExtCheck|Checkbox_TooltipEnable the dialog again at Tools > Options > General␀OptLinguPageSpecifies the properties of the spelling, thesaurus and hyphenation.␀OptNewDictionaryDialogIn the Dictionary section you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.␀OptPathsPageThis section contains the default paths to important folders of the office suite. These paths can be edited by the user.␀OptSavePageIn the General section, you can select default settings for saving documents, and can select default file formats.␀RID_COLOR_SCHEME_LIBREOFFICE_AUTOMATICAutomatic␀RID_CUISTR_A11Y_DESC_BACKUPSpecifies if the backup copy should be stored in the same folder as the original document. If not selected, the backup copy is stored in the folder specified in Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths - Backups.␀RID_CUISTR_CLICK_RESULT(Click on any test to view its resultant bitmap image)␀RID_CUISTR_OPT_READONLYThis property is locked for editing.␀RID_CUISTR_SAVEDThe results have been successfully saved in the file 'GraphicTestResults.zip'!␀RID_CUISTR_ZIPFAILCreation of ZIP file failed.␀RID_CUI_PERSONAS_COLORDark␀RID_CUI_PERSONAS_COLORGray␀RID_CUI_PERSONAS_COLORGreen␀RID_CUI_PERSONAS_COLORPink␀RID_CUI_PERSONAS_COLORSand␀RID_CUI_PERSONAS_COLORWhite␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%MOD1+Shift+F9 recalculates all formulas in all spreadsheets.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME Calc does not calculate from left to right but respects the order Parentheses – Exponents – Multiplication – Division – Addition – Subtraction.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME allows you to use assistive tools, such as external screen readers, Braille devices or speech recognition input devices.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME can automatically add a numbered caption when you insert objects. See Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME Writer ▸ AutoCaption.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME has a portable version which gives you mobility. Even without administrator rights on your computer you can install %PRODUCTNAME Portable to your hard drive too.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME has a template center to create good looking documents—check it out.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME has great extensions to increase your productivity—check them out.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME helps you not to enter two or more spaces in Writer. Check Tools ▸ AutoCorrect ▸ AutoCorrect Options ▸ Options ▸ Ignore double spaces.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME is developed by a friendly community, made up of hundreds of contributors around the world. Join us with your skills beyond coding.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME offers a variety of user interface options to make you feel at home␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME supports four macro security levels (from low to very high) and trusted sources.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAY%PRODUCTNAME supports over 150 languages.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYAdd background images to spreadsheets via Insert ▸ Image or drag a background from the Gallery, then Format ▸ Arrange ▸ To Background.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYAnnoyed by the “marching ants” around cells in Calc? Press escape to stop them; the copied content will remain available for pasting.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYApart from table of contents, %PRODUCTNAME can create Alphabetical, Illustrations, Tables, Objects, Bibliography, User-Defined indexes.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYApply Heading paragraph styles in Writer with shortcut keys: %MOD1+1 applies Heading 1, %MOD1+2 applies Heading 2, etc.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYAutomatically mark alphabetical index entries using a concordance file.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYBatch-convert your Microsoft Office documents to the OpenDocument format by using the Document Converter wizard in menu File ▸ Wizards ▸ Document Converter.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYBest way to fix bad-looking MS Word table cells via Table ▸ Size ▸ Optimal Row Height / Column Width.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYCalculate loan repayments with Calc: eg. PMT(2%/12;36;2500) interest rate per payment period 2%/12, 36 months, loan amount 2500.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYCannot find what you want with the VLOOKUP function in Calc? With INDEX and MATCH you can do anything!␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYCannot see all the text in a cell? Expand the input line in the formula bar and you can scroll.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYCan’t find a command in the menus? Try Shift+ESC.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYChange the basic fonts for the predefined template or current document per Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME Writer ▸ Basic Fonts.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYChoose “Hierarchical View” in the Styles sidebar to see the relation between styles.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYClick a column field (row) PivotTable and press F12 to group data. Choices adapt to content: Date (month, quarter, year), number (classes)␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYClick on the special character icon in the toolbar to get quick access to favorite and recent characters to insert.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYConstruct your own 2D shapes in Draw. Select two or more objects, and explore possibilities with Shape ▸ Combine, Shape ▸ Merge, Shape ▸ Subtract, and Shape ▸ Intersect.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYCustomize footnote appearance with Tools ▸ Footnote/Endnote Settings…␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYData ▸ Validity allows you to create drop-down lists where the user selects a value instead of typing.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDate/time value is just a number of days since a chosen day zero; in the number, integer part represents date, and fractional part is time (elapsed part of a day), with 0.5 representing noon.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDefine texts that you often use as AutoText. You will be able to insert them by their name, shortcut or toolbar in any Writer document.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDelete all of your printing areas in one step: select all sheets, then Format ▸ Print Ranges ▸ Clear.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDeveloping new XSLT and XML filters?␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDid you know that you can attach comments to portions of text? Just use the shortcut %MOD1+%MOD2+C.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDisplay photos or images with different shapes in Writer. Insert and select shape, then Insert ▸ Image. To adjust image, right-click on selected shape and choose Area.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDo not get lost in large documents. Use the Navigator (F5) to find your way through the content.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDo not insert manual breaks to separate two paragraphs. Rather change Indents & Spacing ▸ Spacing ▸ Below paragraph at the style/paragraph properties.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDo not use tabs to space items on a Writer document. Depending on what you are trying to do, a borderless table can be a better choice.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDo you plan to change your computer and want to recover your customizations? See:␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDon’t like the position of some icons on your toolbar? Change it with Tools ▸ Customize ▸ Toolbars tab ▸ Target.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDrag & drop cells from Calc into the normal view of a slide creates a table; into the outline view, each cell creates a line in the outline.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYDrag a formatted object to the Styles and Formatting window. A dialog box opens, just enter the name of the new style.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYEasily convert your documents to PDF with one click by clicking on the PDF icon in the toolbar.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYEdit ▸ Find and Replace lets you insert special characters directly: right click in input fields or press Shift+%MOD1+S.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYEmbedded help is available by pressing F1, if you have installed it. Otherwise check online at:␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYEnable massive parallel calculations of formula cells via Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME ▸ OpenCL.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYExplore the ten different functions in the status bar (at the bottom of the document window). Place the cursor over each field for an explanation. If not visible, use View ▸ Status Bar.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYFind all expressions in brackets per Edit ▸ Find and Replace ▸ Find ▸ \([^)]+\) (check “Regular expressions”)␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYFit the entire page in a Draw window, use * on the number pad.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYFit your sheet or print ranges to a page with Format ▸ Page ▸ Sheet Tab ▸ Scaling Mode.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYFor quick access to your document bookmarks, right-click on the page number of the status bar (lower-left corner of document window).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYFrames can be linked so that the text can flow from one to the other as in desktop publishing.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYGenerate fully customized PDF documents with the exact format, image compression, comments, access rights, password, etc., via File ▸ Export as PDF.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYGet %PRODUCTNAME documentation and free user guide books at:␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYGet help from the community via the Ask portal.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYGot many images in your Writer document? Speed up the display by disabling View ▸ Images and charts.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYHaving trouble pasting text from PDF files or webpages into documents? Try to paste as unformatted text (%MOD1+%MOD2+Shift+V).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYHold down %MOD1 and turn the mouse wheel to change the zoom factor.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYIn %PRODUCTNAME Draw to change the 0/0 point of the rulers, drag the intersection of the two rulers in the top left corner into the workspace.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYIn %PRODUCTNAME Impress, use Insert ▸ Media ▸ Photo Album to create a slideshow from a series of pictures with the “Photo Album” feature.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYIn Calc use TRIMMEAN() to return the mean of a data set excluding the highest and lowest values.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYIn a Draw page, use “-” to zoom out; “+” to zoom in.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYIn the replace input field of auto correct options you can use the wildcards .*␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYInclude a paragraph that is not a heading in the “Table of Contents” by giving a numerical outline level to the paragraph in the “Outline & List” tab in the paragraph settings.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYInsert and number your formulas in one step: type fn then F3. An AutoText is inserted with formula and number aligned in a table.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYInsert images and photos into shapes in Draw and Impress. Right-click on a shape, choose Area ▸ Image ▸ Add / Import, and use Options to adjust appearance.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYInsert your metadata in your document with Insert ▸ Fields ▸ More Fields… ▸ Document or DocInformation.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYKeep column headers of a sheet visible when scrolling lines via View ▸ Freeze Cells ▸ Freeze First Row.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYKeep the zeros before a number by using the “leading zeroes” cell format option or format the cell as text before entering the number.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYLeft-handed? Enable Tools ▸ Options ▸ Languages and Locales ▸ General ▸ Asian and check Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME Writer ▸ View ▸ Ruler ▸ Right-aligned, which displays the scrollbar to the left.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYMix portrait and landscape orientations in a Calc spreadsheet by applying different page styles on sheets.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYMove a column in Calc between two others in one step? Click the header then a cell in the column, keep mouse button and move to the target with %MOD2 key.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNeed custom contents for metadata properties? File ▸ Properties ▸ Custom Properties tab lets you create what you want.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNeed to allow changes to parts of a read-only document in Writer? Insert frames or sections that can authorize changes.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNeed to do citation? You can use third-party citation managers such as Zotero.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNeed to include a list item without a bullet or number? Use “Insert Unnumbered Entry” in the Bullets and Numbering toolbar.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNeed to insert the date in a spreadsheet cell? Type %MOD1+; or Shift+%MOD1+; to insert the time.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNeed to move a Writer table? Table ▸ Select ▸ Table and Insert ▸ Frame ▸ Frame and move where you want.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNeed to move one or more paragraphs? No need to cut and paste: Use the keyboard shortcut %MOD1+%MOD2+Arrow (Up/Down)␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNeed to position precisely? %MOD2+arrow keys move objects (shapes, pictures, formulas) by one pixel.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNeed to present a report written with Writer? File ▸ Send ▸ Outline to Presentation automatically creates a slideshow from the outline.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNever use certain arrow styles? Remove them by using the Delete button on the Format ▸ Text Box and Shape ▸ Line ▸ Arrow Styles tab.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNew versions of %PRODUCTNAME provide new features, bug fixes, and security patches. Keep your software updated!␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYNo need to scroll through the list at Tools ▸ Customize ▸ Keyboard to find a shortcut: just type it.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYOften create one document from another? Consider using a template.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYOpen a CSV file as a new sheet in the current spreadsheet via Sheet ▸ Sheet from file.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYOptimize your table layout with Table ▸ Size ▸ Distribute Rows / Columns Evenly.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYPlay music throughout a slideshow by assigning the sound to the first slide transition without clicking the “Apply to All Slides” button.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYPress Shift+F1 to see any available extended tooltips in dialog boxes, when "Extended tips" is not enabled in Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME ▸ General.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYRename your slides in Impress to help you define “Go to page” interactions and to have a summary more explicit than Slide1, Slide2…␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYRight-click in the status bar in %PRODUCTNAME Calc and select “Selection count” to display the number of selected cells.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYRun %PRODUCTNAME in any browser via rollApp.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYSelect a different icon set from Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME ▸ View ▸ Icon Theme.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYSelect an object in the document background via the Select tool in the Drawing toolbar to surround the object to select.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYSelect options in Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME Writer ▸ Formatting Aids ▸ Display Formatting to specify which non-printing characters are displayed.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYShift+%MOD1+Del deletes from cursor to the end of the current sentence.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYShow or hide comments in Writer by clicking the comment toggle button in the ruler.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYStrange error code in Calc, Err: followed by a number? This page gives the explanation:␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYThe 4th optional parameter of VLOOKUP Calc function indicates whether the first column of data is sorted. If not, enter FALSE or zero.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYThe presenter console is a great feature when working with %PRODUCTNAME Impress. Have you checked it out?␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo automatically number table rows in Writer, select the relevant column, then apply a List Style.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo change the number of a page in Writer, go to the properties of the first paragraph and at the Text Flow tab check Break ▸ Insert and enter the number.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo convert a formula into static values you do not need to copy/paste; use Data ▸ Calculate ▸ Formula to Value.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo copy a comment without losing the content of the target cell you should use Paste Special and uncheck everything except “Comments” in dialog. Use Operations “Add” to not override existing content.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo delete multiple comments, select cells with comments and use Sheet ▸ Cell Comments ▸ Delete Comment.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo display the scrollbar to the left, enable Tools ▸ Options ▸ Languages and Locales ▸ General ▸ Complex text and right click a sheet in Sheet tabs above Status bar ▸ Right-To-Left.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo distribute some text in multi-columns select the text and apply Format ▸ Columns.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo enable macro recording, check Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME ▸ Advanced ▸ Enable macro recording.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo get the “Vertical Text” tool in the Drawing toolbar, check Tools ▸ Options ▸ Languages and Locales ▸ General ▸ Default languages for Documents ▸ Asian (and make the button visible with right-click and then Visible Buttons ▸ Vertical Text).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo insert a paragraph before (after) a section, press %MOD2+Enter at the beginning (end) of the section.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo insert the current date in your document, use Insert ▸ Field ▸ Date.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo modify an AutoPlay presentation, open it and after it starts, right click and select Edit in the context menu.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo print the notes of your slides go to File ▸ Print ▸ %PRODUCTNAME Impress tab and select Notes under Document ▸ Type.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo quickly zoom in on range selection, right click on the zoom part of the status bar and choose Optimal.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo remove a hyperlink but keep its text, right-click on the hyperlink, and use “Remove Hyperlink”.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo remove several hyperlinks at once, select the text with the hyperlinks, then right-click and use “Remove Hyperlink”.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo remove the page number from your table of contents go to Insert ▸ Table of Contents and Index (or right-click and Edit Index to edit a previously inserted index). In the Entries tab delete the page number (#) from Structure line.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo repeat a table heading when a table spans over a page, use Table ▸ Table Properties ▸ Text Flow ▸ Repeat heading.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo repeat rows/columns on every pages use Format ▸ Print Ranges ▸ Edit.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo search in several spreadsheets, select them before you start the search.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo select a contiguous range of cells containing data and bounded by empty row and columns use %MOD1+* (numeric key pad).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo start temporarily with a fresh user profile, or to restore a non-working %PRODUCTNAME, use Help ▸ Restart in Safe Mode.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTo zoom a selection to fit the entire window in Draw, use the / (divide key) on the number pad.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYToolbars are contextual—they open depending on the context. If you do not want that, uncheck them from View ▸ Toolbars.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTools ▸ Detective ▸ Mark Invalid Data highlights all cells in the sheet that contain values outside the validation rules.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTrace cells used in a formula, precedents (Shift+F9) or dependents (Shift+F5) (or use Tools ▸ Detective). For each hit you go one more step in the chain.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYTranspose a Writer table? Copy and paste in Calc, transpose with copy/paste special then copy/paste special ▸ Formatted text in Writer.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUnable to modify or delete a custom cell style? Check all sheets, none should be protected.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUncheck Slide Show ▸ Settings ▸ Presentation always on top if you need another program displays its window to the front of your presentation.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUncheck Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME Calc ▸ View ▸ Zoom: “Synchronize sheets” so that each sheet in Calc has its own zoom factor.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse %MOD1+%MOD2+Shift+V to paste the contents of the clipboard as unformatted text.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse Data ▸ Statistics for sampling, descriptive statistics, analysis of variance, correlation, and much more in %PRODUCTNAME Calc.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse Format ▸ Align Objects in Impress or Shape ▸ Align Objects in Draw (or the context menu) for precise positioning of objects: it centers on the page if one object is selected or works on the group respectively.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse Format ▸ Conditional Formatting ▸ Manage in Calc to find out which cells have been defined with conditional formatting.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse Page/Slide ▸ Properties ▸ “Fit object to paper format” in Draw/Impress to resize the objects so that they fit on your chosen paper format.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse Sheet ▸ Fill Cells ▸ Random Number to generate a random series based on various distributions.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse Shift+Space to select the current row and %MOD1+Space to select the current column.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse View ▸ Value Highlighting to display cell contents in colors: Text/black, Formulas/green, Numbers/blue, Protected cells/grey background.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse column or row labels in formulas. For example, if you have two columns, “Time” and “KM”, use =Time/KM to get minutes per kilometer.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse font embedding for greater interoperability with other office suites at File ▸ Properties ▸ Font.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse the Backspace key instead of Delete in Calc. You can choose what to delete.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse the Connector tool from the Drawing toolbar in Draw/Impress to create nice flow charts and optionally copy/paste the object into Writer.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYUse your Android or iPhone to remotely control your Impress presentation.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant headings to always begin a page? Edit the paragraph style applied to the headings. Check “Insert” on the “Text Flow” tab, with Type “Page” and Position “Before”.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant the cursor to go into the cell to the right, after entering a value in Calc? Use the Tab key instead of Enter.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to add many of the same shapes in Draw/Impress? Double-click a tool in the drawing toolbar to use it for repeated tasks.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to become a %PRODUCTNAME Ambassador? There are certifications for developers, admins, and trainers.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to center cells on a printed page in Calc? Format ▸ Page, Page ▸ Layout settings ▸ Table alignment.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to change spell checking for some part of the text? Click in the language zone of the status bar or better, apply a style.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to count words for just one particular paragraph style? Use Edit ▸ Find and Replace, click Paragraph Styles, select the style in Find, and click Find All. Read the result in the status bar.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to display only the highest values in a spreadsheet? Select menu Data ▸ AutoFilter, click the drop-down arrow, and choose “Top10”.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to display text before a heading number? Open the Numbering tab of the “Heading Numbering” dialog and enter the desired text in “Before”. For example, type “Chapter ” to display “Chapter 1”.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to duplicate the above line? Press %MOD1+D or use Sheet ▸ Fill Cells ▸ Fill Down.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to export formulas to CSV? File ▸ Save As ▸ Type:Text CSV, check “Edit filter settings”, and check “Save cell formulas” in the next dialog.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to find the words in bold in a Writer document? Edit ▸ Find and Replace ▸ Other options ▸ Attributes ▸ Font weight.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to find words containing more than 10 characters? Edit ▸ Find and Replace ▸ Search ▸ [a-z]{10,} ▸ Other Options ▸ check Regular expressions.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to get a math object into Writer quickly? Type your formula, select it, and use Insert ▸ OLE Object ▸ Formula to convert the text.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to have two or more columns for just a part of a %PRODUCTNAME Writer page? Insert ▸ Section, set with Columns tab, and place text in that section.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to hide some text in a document? Select the text. Insert ▸ Section, and select “Hide”.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to insert a placeholder for an image in a Writer template? Use Insert ▸ Fields ▸ More fields, click Functions tab, choose PlaceHolder for Type and Image for Format.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to insert a value in the same place on several sheets? Select the sheets: hold down %MOD1 key and click their tabs before entering.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to jump to a particular page by its number? Click the left-most statusbar entry or use Edit ▸ Go To Page… or press %MOD1+G.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to keep a part of an editable document as read-only? Insert ▸ Section. Add text to the section, then right-click “Edit Section” and check “Protect”.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to know how many days there are in the current month? Use the DAYSINMONTH(TODAY()) function.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to know if a cell is referred in formulas of other cells? Tools ▸ Detective ▸ Trace Dependents (Shift+F5).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to know the valid command line parameters? Start soffice with --help or -h or -?␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to manage the presentation of hyperlinks in a spreadsheet? Insert them with the HYPERLINK function.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to open hyperlinks without pressing the %MOD1 key? Uncheck “%MOD1+click required to open hyperlinks” in Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME ▸ Security ▸ Options ▸ Security Options.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to print two portrait pages on a landscape one (reducing A4 to A5)? File ▸ Print and select 2 at “Pages per sheet”.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to quickly insert or delete rows? Select the desired number of rows (or columns) and press %MOD1+Plus sign (+) to add or %MOD1+Minus sign (-) to delete.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to remove all <> at once and keep the text inside? Edit ▸ Find and Replace: Search = [<>], Replace = blank and check “Regular expressions” under Other options.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to return to default after applying a list style? Click Bullets or Numbering On/Off tool on the Formatting toolbar.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to see, but not print, an object in Draw? Draw it on a layer for which the “Printable” flag is not set (right-click the layer’s tab and choose “Modify Layer”).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to select a large range of cells without scrolling? Type the range reference (e.g. A1:A1000) in the name box then Enter.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to show hidden column A? Click a cell in column B, press the left mouse button, move the mouse to the left, release. Then switch it on via Format ▸ Columns ▸ Show.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to show the contents of another document within your document? Use Insert ▸ Section and select Link.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to sort a pivot table? Click on drop-list’s arrow in the row/col header and select sort method: ascending, descending, or custom.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to sort a series in %PRODUCTNAME Calc such as A1, A2, A3, A11, A15, not in alphabetical order but on the number? Enable natural sort in the Options tab.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWant to sum a cell through several sheets? Refer to the range of sheets e.g. =SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWhen editing a cell in place, you can right click and Insert fields: Date, Sheet name, Document title, etc.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWhen you have created a Style based on another, you can enter a percentage value or a point value (e.g. 110% or −2pt or +5pt).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWith %PRODUCTNAME it is very easy to install a new dictionary: they are supplied as extensions.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWith %PRODUCTNAME you can use your Google Mail account to do a mail merge. Fill in Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME Writer ▸ Mail Merge Email.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWith Slide Show ▸ Custom Slide Show, reorder and pick slides to fit a slideshow to the needs of your viewers.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWith Tools ▸ AutoText ▸ AutoText ▸ Import you can select a Word document or a template containing the AutoText entries that you want to import.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWith the Navigator you can select & move up/down headings and the text below the heading, in the Navigator and in the document.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWrite along a curve? Draw the curve, double click, type the text, Format ▸ Text Box and Shape ▸ Fontwork. Select one of the alignment options: Rotate, Upright, Slant Horizontal or Slant Vertical.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWriter can insert a blank page between two odd (even) pages that follow. Check “Print automatically inserted blank pages” in the print dialog’s %PRODUCTNAME Writer tab.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWriter helps you to make backups: with File ▸ Save a Copy you create a new document continuing to work on the original.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWriter includes LibreLogo: simple Logo-like programming environment with turtle vector graphics, DTP and graphic design.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWriter lets you number your footnotes per page, chapter, document: Tools ▸ Footnote/Endnote Settings ▸ Footnotes tab ▸ Counting.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYWriting a book? %PRODUCTNAME master document lets you manage large documents as a container for individual %PRODUCTNAME Writer files.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can change the default function in the status bar: right click on the area.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can change the look of %PRODUCTNAME via View ▸ User Interface.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can continue writing with the default formatting attributes after manually applying bold, italic or underline by pressing %MOD1+Shift+X.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can copy from one sheet to another without the clipboard. Select the area to copy, %MOD1+click the target sheet’s tab and use Sheet ▸ Fill Cells ▸ Fill Sheets.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can create a chart based on a Writer table by clicking in the table and choosing Insert ▸ Chart.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can create a master document from the current Writer document by using File ▸ Send ▸ Create Master Document.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can create an illustration index from object names, not only from captions.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can create different master pages in a presentation template: View ▸ Master Slide and Slide ▸ New Master (or per toolbar or right click in slide pane).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can create editable Hybrid PDFs with %PRODUCTNAME.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can create fillable form documents (even PDFs) with %PRODUCTNAME.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can customize the middle mouse button by going to Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME ▸ View ▸ Mouse ▸ Middle button.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can display a number as a fraction (0.125 = 1/8): Format ▸ Cells, under Numbers tab in the Category select Fraction.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can move an object to another layer by holding it until its edges flash, then drag it to the tab of the layer you want to move it to.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can protect cells with Format ▸ Cells ▸ Protection. To prevent insert, delete, rename, move/copy of sheets use Tools ▸ Protect Sheet.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can reformat all comments in a document by clicking the down arrow in a comment and choose “Format all Comments”.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can restart the slide show after a pause specified at Slide Show ▸ Slide Show Settings ▸ Loop and repeat after.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can rotate cells table orientation with Table ▸ Properties… ▸ Text Flow ▸ Text orientation.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can set a color for each tab: right-click the tab or use Sheet ▸ Sheet Tab Color.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can show formulas instead of results with View ▸ Show Formula (or Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME Calc ▸ View ▸ Display ▸ Formulas).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can sign existing PDF files and also verify those signatures.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can sort paragraphs or table rows alphabetically or numerically per Tools ▸ Sort.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can toggle between the field names and the actual value with View ▸ Fields Names (or %MOD1+F9).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou can use styles to make the tables in your document consistent. Choose one from the predefined per Styles (F11) or via Table ▸ AutoFormat Styles...␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou do not want to print all columns? Hide or group the ones you do not need.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou need to fill a series? Select the cell range and Sheet ▸ Fill Cells ▸ Fill Series and choose between Linear, Growth, Date and AutoFill.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou want to add x months to a date? Use =EDATE(date;months).␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou want to start working with Basic macros? Take a look at the examples under Tools ▸ Macros ▸ Edit Macros.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYou would like to view the calculation of individual elements of a formula, select the respective elements and press F9.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYour Writer document does not reopen with the text cursor at the same editing position it was when you saved it? Add First or Last name in Tools ▸ Options ▸ %PRODUCTNAME ▸ User Data ▸ First/last name.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYour date acceptance pattern is inappropriate? Use Tools ▸ Options ▸ Languages and Locales ▸ General ▸ Date acceptance patterns to tweak the pattern.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYour donations support our worldwide community.␀RID_CUI_TIPOFTHEDAYYour numbers are displayed as ### in your spreadsheet? The column is too narrow to display all digits.␀RID_CUI_TOOLBARMODESStandard user interface but with single-line toolbar. Intended for use on small screens.␀RID_CUI_TOOLBARMODESStandard user interface with expanded sidebar. Expert users who want to quickly change many different properties are advised to use this UI.␀RID_CUI_TOOLBARMODESStandard user interface with menu, toolbar, and collapsed sidebar. Intended for users who are familiar with the classic interface.␀RID_CUI_TOOLBARMODESThe Contextual Groups interface focuses on beginners. It exposes the most frequently used functions on groups with the core action as large icon and a couple of small additional features. All functions have a label. Depending on the context, an additional section provides access to those functions.␀RID_CUI_TOOLBARMODESThe Contextual Single interface shows functions in a single-line toolbar with context-dependent content.␀RID_CUI_TOOLBARMODESThe Groupedbar interface provides access to functions in groups, with icons for most-frequently used features, and dropdown menus for others. This compact variant favors vertical space.␀RID_CUI_TOOLBARMODESThe Groupedbar interface provides access to functions in groups, with icons for most-frequently used features, and dropdown menus for others. This full variant favors functions and is slightly larger than others.␀RID_CUI_TOOLBARMODESThe Tabbed Compact variant aims to be familiar with the Microsoft Office interface, yet occupying less space for smaller screens.␀RID_CUI_TOOLBARMODESThe Tabbed user interface is the most similar to the Ribbons used in Microsoft Office. It organizes functions in tabs and makes the main menu obsolete.␀RID_LANGUAGETOOL_LEAVE_EMPTYLeave this field empty to use the free version␀RID_LANGUAGETOOL_REST_LEAVE_EMPTYLeave this field empty to use LanguageTool protocol␀RID_MULTIPATH_DBL_ERRThe path %1 already exists.␀RID_STR_FROM_BOTTOMFrom bottom␀RID_STR_FROM_TOPFrom top␀RID_STR_OVERFLOW_BACKWARDOverflow, search continued at the end␀RID_STR_OVERFLOW_FORWARDOverflow, search continued at the beginning␀RID_STR_SEARCH_ANYWHEREanywhere in the field␀RID_STR_SEARCH_BEGINNINGbeginning of field␀RID_STR_SEARCH_COUNTINGcounting records␀RID_STR_SEARCH_ENDend of field␀RID_STR_SEARCH_GENERAL_ERRORAn unknown error occurred. The search could not be finished.␀RID_STR_SEARCH_NORECORDNo records corresponding to your data found.␀RID_STR_SEARCH_WHOLEentire field␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDAdd␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_DIALOG_TITLE_PREFIXExtensions␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_DICTIONARYExtensions: Dictionary␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_GALLERYExtensions: Gallery␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_ICONSExtensions: Icons␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_INSTALLBUTTONInstall␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_INSTALLEDBUTTONInstalled␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_INSTALLINGInstalling␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_LOADINGLoading...␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_PALETTESExtensions: Color Palette␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_SEARCHINGSearching...␀RID_SVXSTR_ADDITIONS_TEMPLATESExtensions: Templates␀RID_SVXSTR_ADD_FAVORITESAdd to Favorites␀RID_SVXSTR_ADD_IMAGEAdd Image␀RID_SVXSTR_ADD_SUBMENUAdd Submenu␀RID_SVXSTR_ALLFUNCTIONSAll commands␀RID_SVXSTR_ALL_COMMANDSAll Commands␀RID_SVXSTR_ANGLE_QUOTESReplace two inequality signs (<< or >>) with angle quotes␀RID_SVXSTR_ARCHIVE_HEADLINEArchives␀RID_SVXSTR_ARCHIVE_TITLESelect Archives␀RID_SVXSTR_ASK_CHANGE_LINESTYLEThe line style was modified without saving. 
