t to the full width of the drawing object or text object.␀textattrtabpage|extended_tip|TSB_WORDWRAP_TEXTWraps the text that you add after double-clicking a custom shape to fit inside the shape.␀textattrtabpage|extended_tip|TextAttributesPageSets the layout and anchoring properties for text in the selected drawing or text object.␀textattrtabpage|label1Drawing Object Text␀textattrtabpage|label2Spacing to Borders␀textattrtabpage|label3Text Anchor␀textattrtabpage|label4_Left:␀textattrtabpage|label5_Right:␀textattrtabpage|label6_Top:␀textattrtabpage|label7_Bottom:␀textattrtabpage|label8Custom Shape Text␀textcolumnstabpage|extended_tip|FLD_COL_NUMBEREnter the number of columns to use for the text.␀textcolumnstabpage|extended_tip|MTR_FLD_COL_SPACINGEnter the amount of space to leave between the columns.␀textcolumnstabpage|extended_tip|TextColumnsPageSets the columns’ layout properties for text in the selected drawing or text object.␀textcolumnstabpage|labelColNumber_Number of columns:␀textcolumnstabpage|labelColSpacing_Spacing:␀textdialog|RID_SVXPAGE_TEXTANIMATIONText Animation␀textdialog|RID_SVXPAGE_TEXTATTRText␀textdialog|RID_SVXPAGE_TEXTCOLUMNSText Columns␀textdialog|TextDialogText␀textflowpage|LabelHyphenationHyphenation␀textflowpage|checkAutoA_utomatically␀textflowpage|checkInsert_Insert␀textflowpage|checkKeepPara_Keep with next paragraph␀textflowpage|checkNoCapsDon't hyphenate words in _CAPS␀textflowpage|checkNoLastWordDon't hyphenate the last word␀textflowpage|checkOrphanNo split at _beginning of paragraph␀textflowpage|checkOrphanNumber of lines, that will be kept together at the beginning of the paragraph (orphan control).␀textflowpage|checkOrphanNumber of lines, that will be kept together at the end of the paragraph (widow control).␀textflowpage|checkPageStyleWith page st_yle:␀textflowpage|checkSplitPara_Allow to split paragraph␀textflowpage|checkWidowNo split at _end of paragraph␀textflowpage|comboBreakPositionAfter␀textflowpage|comboBreakPositionBefore␀textflowpage|comboBreakTypeColumn␀textflowpage|comboBreakTypePage␀textflowpage|comboPageStyle-atkobjectPage Style␀textflowpage|extended_tip|TextFlowPageSpecify hyphenation and pagination options.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|checkAutoAutomatically inserts hyphens where they are needed in a paragraph.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|checkInsertSelect this check box, and then select the break type that you want to use.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|checkKeepParaKeeps the current paragraph and the following paragraph together when a break or column break is inserted.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|checkOrphanSpecifies the minimum number of lines in a paragraph before a page break. Select this check box, and then enter a number in the Lines box.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|checkPageStyleSelect this check box, and then select the page style that you want to use for the first page after the break.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|checkSplitParaShifts the entire paragraph to the next page or column after a break is inserted.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|checkWidowSpecifies the minimum number of lines in a paragraph in the first page after the break. Select this check box, and then enter a number in the Lines box.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|comboBreakPositionSelect where you want to insert the break.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|comboBreakTypeSelect the break type that you want to insert.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|comboPageStyleSelect the formatting style to use for the first page after the break.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|spinLineBeginEnter the minimum number of characters that must appear at the beginning of the line after the hyphen.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|spinLineEndEnter the minimum number of characters to leave at the end of the line before a hyphen is inserted.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|spinMaxNumEnter the maximum number of consecutive lines that can be hyphenated.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|spinMinLenEnter the minimum word length in characters that can be hyphenated.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|spinOrphanSpecifies the minimum number of lines in a paragraph before a page break. Select this check box, and then enter a number in the Lines box.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|spinPageNumberEnter the page number for the first page that follows the break. If you want to continue the current page numbering, leave the checkbox unchecked.␀textflowpage|extended_tip|spinWidowSpecifies the minimum number of lines in a paragraph in the first page after the break. Select this check box, and then enter a number in the Lines box.␀textflowpage|label3Breaks␀textflowpage|labelHyphenZoneHyphenation _zone:␀textflowpage|labelLineBeginCha_racters at line begin␀textflowpage|labelLineEndC_haracters at line end␀textflowpage|labelMaxNum_Maximum consecutive hyphenated lines␀textflowpage|labelMinLen_Minimum word length in characters␀textflowpage|labelOptionsSplit Options␀textflowpage|labelOrphanlines␀textflowpage|labelPageNumPage _number:␀textflowpage|labelPositionPosition:␀textflowpage|labelType_Type:␀textflowpage|labelWidowlines␀thesaurus|RID_SVXSTR_ERR_TEXTNOTFOUNDNo alternatives found.␀thesaurus|ThesaurusDialogThesaurus␀thesaurus|extended_tip|ThesaurusDialogOpens a dialog box to replace the current word with a synonym, or a related term.␀thesaurus|extended_tip|alternativesClick an entry in the Alternatives list to copy the related term to the "Replace with" text box. Double-click an entry to copy the related term to the "Current word" text box and to look up that term.␀thesaurus|extended_tip|langcbSelect a language for the thesaurus.␀thesaurus|extended_tip|leftRecalls the previous contents of the "Current word" text box.␀thesaurus|extended_tip|replaceedThe word or words in the "Replace with" text box will replace the original word in the document when you click the Replace button. You can also type text directly in this box.␀thesaurus|extended_tip|wordcbDisplays the current word, or the related term that you selected by double-clicking a line in the Alternatives list. You can also type text directly in this box to look up your text.␀thesaurus|label1Current word:␀thesaurus|label2Alternatives:␀thesaurus|label3Replace with:␀thesaurus|replace_Replace␀title-atkobjectTitle␀transparencytabpage|CTL_IMAGE_PREVIEW-atkobjectExample␀transparencytabpage|CTL_TRANS_PREVIEW-atkobjectExample␀transparencytabpage|FL_PROPArea Transparency Mode␀transparencytabpage|FT_TRGR_ANGLE_Angle:␀transparencytabpage|FT_TRGR_BORDERTransition start:␀transparencytabpage|FT_TRGR_CENTER_XCenter _X:␀transparencytabpage|FT_TRGR_CENTER_YCenter _Y:␀transparencytabpage|FT_TRGR_END_VALUE_End value:␀transparencytabpage|FT_TRGR_START_VALUE_Start value:␀transparencytabpage|FT_TRGR_TYPETy_pe:␀transparencytabpage|RBT_TRANS_GRADIENT_Gradient␀transparencytabpage|RBT_TRANS_LINEAR_Transparency:␀transparencytabpage|RBT_TRANS_OFF_No transparency␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|LB_TRGR_GRADIENT_TYPESSelect the type of transparency gradient that you want to apply.␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|MTR_TRANSPARENTAdjusts the transparency of the current fill color. Enter a number between 0% (opaque) and 100% (transparent).␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|MTR_TRGR_ANGLEEnter a rotation angle for the gradient.␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|MTR_TRGR_BORDEREnter the amount by which you want to adjust the transparent area of the gradient. The default value is 0%.␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|MTR_TRGR_CENTER_XEnter the horizontal offset for the gradient.␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|MTR_TRGR_CENTER_YEnter the vertical offset for the gradient.␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|MTR_TRGR_END_VALUEEnter a transparency value for the endpoint of the gradient, where 0% is fully opaque and 100% is fully transparent.␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|MTR_TRGR_START_VALUEEnter a transparency value for the beginning point of the gradient, where 0% is fully opaque and 100% is fully transparent.␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|RBT_TRANS_GRADIENTApplies a transparency gradient to the current fill color. Select this option, and then set the gradient properties.␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|RBT_TRANS_LINEARTurns on color transparency. Select this option, and then enter a number in the box, where 0% is fully opaque and 100% is fully transparent.␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|RBT_TRANS_OFFTurns off color transparency.␀transparencytabpage|extended_tip|TransparencyTabPageSet the transparency options for the fill that you apply to the selected object.␀transparencytabpage|liststoreTYPEAxial␀transparencytabpage|liststoreTYPEEllipsoid␀transparencytabpage|liststoreTYPELinear␀transparencytabpage|liststoreTYPERadial␀transparencytabpage|liststoreTYPERectangular␀transparencytabpage|liststoreTYPESquare (Quadratic)␀tsaurldialog|TSAURLDialogTime Stamping Authority URLs␀tsaurldialog|add_Add...␀tsaurldialog|enteraurlEnter a Time Stamp Authority URL␀tsaurldialog|label1TSA URL␀tsaurldialog|label2Add or delete Time Stamp Authority URLs␀twolinespage|label2Double-lined␀twolinespage|label28Enclosing Characters␀twolinespage|label29Initial character␀twolinespage|label30Final character␀twolinespage|liststore1(␀twolinespage|liststore1(None)␀twolinespage|liststore1<␀twolinespage|liststore1Other Characters...␀twolinespage|liststore1[␀twolinespage|liststore1{␀twolinespage|liststore2(None)␀twolinespage|liststore2)␀twolinespage|liststore2>␀twolinespage|liststore2Other Characters...␀twolinespage|liststore2]␀twolinespage|liststore2}␀twolinespage|preview-atkobjectPreview␀twolinespage|twolinesWrite in double lines␀typeThe type of code to generate.␀upIncreases the priority of the module selected in the list box by one level.␀warnalienformatYou can choose to get a warning message when you save a document in a format that is not OpenDocument or which you did not set as default format in Load/Save - General in the Options dialog box.␀widgettestdialog|WidgetTestDialogTest Widgets␀wordYou can type a new word for inclusion in the dictionary. In the list below you will see the contents of the current custom dictionary.␀wordcompletionpage|appendspace_Append space␀wordcompletionpage|collectwordsC_ollect words␀wordcompletionpage|delete_Delete␀wordcompletionpage|enablewordcompleteEnable word _completion␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|WordCompletionPageStores frequently used words, and automatically completes a word after you type three letters that match the first three letters of a stored word.␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|acceptwithSelect the key that you want to use to accept the automatic word completion.␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|appendspaceIf you do not add punctuation after the word then a space is added automatically.␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|collectwordsAdds the frequently used words to a list. To remove a word from the Word Completion list, select the word, and then click Delete Entry.␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|deleteRemoves the selected word or words from the Word Completion list.␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|enablewordcompleteStores frequently used words, and automatically completes a word after you type three letters that match the first three letters of a stored word.␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|entriesLists the collected words. The list is valid until you close the current document. To make the list available to other documents in the current session, disable "When closing a document, remove the words collected from it from the list".␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|maxentriesEnter the maximum number of words that you want to store in the Word Completion list.␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|minwordlenEnter the minimum word length for a word to become eligible for the word completion feature.␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|showastipDisplays the completed word as a Help Tip.␀wordcompletionpage|extended_tip|whenclosingWhen enabled, the list gets cleared when closing the current document. When disabled, makes the current Word Completion list available to other documents after you close the current document. The list remains available until you exit office suite.␀wordcompletionpage|label1_Max. entries:␀wordcompletionpage|label2Mi_n. word length:␀wordcompletionpage|label3Acc_ept with:␀wordcompletionpage|showastip_Show as tip␀wordcompletionpage|whenclosing_When closing a document, remove the words collected from it from the list␀wordcompletionpage|wordcompletionWord Completion␀wordlengthSpecifies the minimum number of characters required for automatic hyphenation to be applied.␀work-atkobjectWork telephone number␀zip-atkobjectZip code␀zoomdialog|100pc100%␀zoomdialog|ZoomDialogZoom & View Layout␀zoomdialog|automaticAutomatic␀zoomdialog|bookmodeBook mode␀zoomdialog|columnsColumns:␀zoomdialog|columnssb-atkobjectColumns␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|100pcDisplays the document at its actual size.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|ZoomDialogReduces or enlarges the screen display.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|automaticThe automatic view layout displays pages side by side, as many as the zoom factor allows.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|bookmodeIn book mode view layout you see two pages side by side as in an open book. The first page is a right page with an odd page number.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|columnsIn columns view layout you see pages in a given number of columns side by side. Enter the number of columns.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|columnssbIn columns view layout you see pages in a given number of columns side by side. Enter the number of columns.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|fitwDisplays the complete width of the document page. The top and bottom edges of the page may not be visible.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|fitwandhDisplays the entire page on your screen.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|optimalResizes the display to fit the width of the text in the document at the moment the command is started.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|singlepageThe single page view layout displays pages beneath each other, but never side by side.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|variableEnter the zoom factor at which you want to display the document. Enter a percentage in the box.␀zoomdialog|extended_tip|zoomsbEnter the zoom factor at which you want to display the document. Enter a percentage in the box.␀zoomdialog|fitwFit width␀zoomdialog|fitwandhFit width and height␀zoomdialog|label1View Layout␀zoomdialog|label2Zoom Factor␀zoomdialog|optimalOptimal␀zoomdialog|singlepageSingle page␀zoomdialog|variableCustom:␀zoomdialog|zoomsb-atkobjectCustom␀Project-Id-Version: PACKAGE VERSION
