␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀d␀␀␀4␀␀�␀␀␀�␀␀␀�␀␀␀E␀␀␀�␀␀␀\␀␀�␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀�␀␀␀A␀␀�␀␀␀Z␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀-␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀�␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀&␀␀�␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀PDF_PROGRESS_BARExport as PDF␀STR_DEFAULT_FILTER_NAMENew Filter␀STR_DEFAULT_UI_NAMEUntitled␀STR_ERROR_EXPORT_XSLT_NOT_FOUNDThe XSLT for export cannot be found. Please enter a valid path.␀STR_ERROR_FILTER_NAME_EXISTSAn XML filter with the name '%s' already exists. Please enter a different name.␀STR_ERROR_IMPORT_TEMPLATE_NOT_FOUNDThe given import template cannot be found. Please enter a valid path.␀STR_ERROR_IMPORT_XSLT_NOT_FOUNDThe XSLT for import cannot be found. Please enter a valid path.␀STR_ERROR_TYPE_NAME_EXISTSThe name for the user interface '%s1' is already used by the XML filter '%s2'. Please enter a different name.␀STR_ERR_PDF_EXPORT_ABORTEDPDF export aborted␀STR_ERR_SIGNATURE_FAILEDSignature generation failed␀STR_EXPORT_ONLYexport filter␀STR_FILTERS_HAVE_BEEN_SAVED%s XML filters have been saved in the package '%s'.␀STR_FILTERS_INSTALLED%s XML filters have been installed successfully.␀STR_FILTER_DOC_LOADINGLoading: ␀STR_FILTER_DOC_SAVINGSaving: ␀STR_FILTER_HAS_BEEN_SAVEDThe XML filter '%s' has been saved as package '%s'. ␀STR_FILTER_INSTALLEDThe XML filter '%s' has been installed successfully.␀STR_FILTER_PACKAGEXSLT filter package␀STR_IMPORT_EXPORTimport/export filter␀STR_IMPORT_ONLYimport filter␀STR_NO_FILTERS_FOUNDNo XML filter could be installed because the package '%s' does not contain any XML filters.␀STR_PDFUA_IGNOREContinue␀STR_PDFUA_INVESTIGATEInvestigate issue␀Investigate issues␀STR_PDF_EXPORT_ODPWDSet permission password␀STR_PDF_EXPORT_UDPWDSet open password␀STR_UNDEFINED_FILTERundefined filter␀STR_UNKNOWN_APPLICATIONUnknown␀STR_WARN_DELETEDo you really want to delete the XML Filter '%s'? This action cannot be undone.␀STR_WARN_FORMACTION_PDFAA form control contained an action not supported by the PDF/A standard. The action was skipped␀STR_WARN_FORMACTION_PDFA_SHORTPDF/A form action␀STR_WARN_PASSWORD_PDFAPDF/A does not allow encryption. The exported PDF file will not be password protected.␀STR_WARN_PDFUA_ISSUESOne accessibility issue detected. Do you want to continue?␀%1 accessibility issues detected. Do you want to continue?␀STR_WARN_TRANSP_CONVERTEDSome objects were converted to an image in order to remove transparencies, because the target PDF format does not support transparencies. Possibly better results can be achieved if you remove the transparent objects before exporting.␀STR_WARN_TRANSP_CONVERTED_SHORTTransparencies removed␀STR_WARN_TRANSP_PDFAPDF/A forbids transparency. A transparent object was painted opaque instead.␀STR_WARN_TRANSP_PDFA_SHORTPDF/A transparency␀STR_WARN_TRANSP_VERSIONTransparency is not supported in PDF versions earlier than PDF 1.4. A transparent object was painted opaque instead␀STR_WARN_TRANSP_VERSION_SHORTPDF version conflict␀STR_XML_FILTER_LISTBOXXML Filter List␀T602FILTER_STR_CANCEL_BUTTONCancel␀T602FILTER_STR_CYRILLIC_MODEMode for Russian language (Cyrillic)␀T602FILTER_STR_DOT_COMMANDSDisplay dot commands␀T602FILTER_STR_ENCODING_AUTOAutomatic␀T602FILTER_STR_ENCODING_CP852CP852 (Latin2)␀T602FILTER_STR_ENCODING_CP895CP895 (KEYB2CS, Kamenicky)␀T602FILTER_STR_ENCODING_KOI8CS2KOI8 CS2␀T602FILTER_STR_ENCODING_LABELEncoding␀T602FILTER_STR_IMPORT_DIALOG_TITLESettings for T602 import␀T602FILTER_STR_OK_BUTTONOK␀T602FILTER_STR_REFORMAT_TEXTReformat the text␀pdfgeneralpage|all_All␀pdfgeneralpage|allowdupsAllow duplicate field _names␀pdfgeneralpage|bookmarksExport outl_ines␀pdfgeneralpage|bookmarks|tooltip_textExport headings along with hyperlinked entries in Table of Contents as PDF bookmarks.␀pdfgeneralpage|comboboxtext-entry75 DPI␀pdfgeneralpage|commentsComm_ents as PDF annotations␀pdfgeneralpage|commentsinmargin_Comments in margin␀pdfgeneralpage|embedHybrid PDF (em_bed ODF file)␀pdfgeneralpage|embed|tooltip_textCreates a PDF that is easily editable in %PRODUCTNAME␀pdfgeneralpage|emptypagesExp_ort automatically inserted blank pages␀pdfgeneralpage|exportplaceholdersExpo_rt placeholders␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|allExports all defined print ranges. If no print range is defined, exports the entire document.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|allowdupsAllows you to use the same field name for multiple fields in the generated PDF file. If disabled, field names will be exported using generated unique names.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|bookmarksPDF bookmarks are created for all paragraphs with outline level 1 or greater and for all “Table of Contents” entries with hyperlinks.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|commentsSelect to export comments of Writer and Calc documents as PDF annotations.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|commentsinmarginSelect to export comments of Writer documents in the page margin.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|embedThis setting enables you to export the document as a .pdf file containing two file formats: PDF and ODF.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|emptypagesIf switched on, automatically inserted blank pages are exported to the PDF file. This is best if you are printing the pdf file double-sided. Example: In a book a chapter paragraph style is set to always start with an odd numbered page. If the previous chapter ends on an odd page, then an even numbered blank page is normally automatically inserted. This option controls whether to export that even numbered page or not.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|exportplaceholdersExport the placeholders fields visual markings only. The exported placeholder is ineffective.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|formatSelect the format of submitting forms from within the PDF file.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|formsChoose to create a PDF form. This can be filled out and printed by the user of the PDF document.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|hiddenpagesExports document hidden slides.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|jpegcompressSelect a JPEG compression level. With a high quality level, almost all pixels are preserved. With a low quality level, some pixels are lost and artifacts are introduced, but file sizes are reduced.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|losslesscompressSelects a lossless compression of images. All pixels are preserved.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|notesExport also the Notes pages view at the end of the exported PDF presentation document.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|onlynotesExports only the Notes page views.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|pagesExports the pages you type in the box.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|pdfaConverts to the PDF/A-2b or PDF/A-1b format. This is defined as an electronic document file format for long term preservation. All fonts that were used in the source document will be embedded into the generated PDF file. PDF tags will be written.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|pdfuaCreates a universal accessibility-complying PDF file that follows the requirements of PDF/UA (ISO 14289) specifications.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|qualityEnter the quality level for JPEG compression.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|rangeExports the pages you type in the box.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|reduceresolutionSelect to resample or down-size the images to a lower number of pixels per inch.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|resolutionSelect the target resolution for the images.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|selectionExports the current selection.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|singlepagessheetsIgnores each sheet’s paper size, print ranges and shown/hidden status and puts every sheet (even hidden sheets) on exactly one page, which is exactly as small or large as needed to fit the whole contents of the sheet.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|taggedSelect to write PDF tags. This can increase file size by huge amounts.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|usereferencexobjectWhen the option is enabled, then the reference XObject markup is used:  viewers have to support this markup to show vector images. Otherwise a fallback bitmap is shown in the viewer.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|viewpdfOpen the exported document in the system default PDF viewer.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|watermarkAdd a centered, vertical, light green watermark text to the page background. The watermark is not part of the source document.␀pdfgeneralpage|extended_tip|watermarkentryInsert the text for the watermark signature.␀pdfgeneralpage|formatFDF␀pdfgeneralpage|formatHTML␀pdfgeneralpage|formatPDF␀pdfgeneralpage|formatXML␀pdfgeneralpage|formsCreate PDF for_m␀pdfgeneralpage|forms|tooltip_textCreates a PDF with fields that can be filled out␀pdfgeneralpage|hiddenpagesExport _hidden pages␀pdfgeneralpage|jpegcompress_JPEG compression␀pdfgeneralpage|label1Range␀pdfgeneralpage|label2Images␀pdfgeneralpage|label3Watermark␀pdfgeneralpage|label4General␀pdfgeneralpage|label6_Quality:␀pdfgeneralpage|label7Submit _format:␀pdfgeneralpage|label9Structure␀pdfgeneralpage|losslesscompress_Lossless compression␀pdfgeneralpage|notesExport _notes pages␀pdfgeneralpage|onlynotesExport onl_y notes pages␀pdfgeneralpage|pdfaArchival (P_DF/A, ISO 19005)␀pdfgeneralpage|pdfaversionPDF_/A version:␀pdfgeneralpage|pdfa|tooltip_textCreates an ISO 19005-2 compliant PDF file, ideal for long-term document preservation␀pdfgeneralpage|pdfuaUniversal Accessibilit_y (PDF/UA)␀pdfgeneralpage|pdfua|tooltip_textCreates a universal accessibility-compliant PDF file that follows the requirements of PDF/UA (ISO 14289) specifications.␀pdfgeneralpage|range_Pages:␀pdfgeneralpage|reduceresolutionReduce ima_ge resolution to:␀pdfgeneralpage|resolution1200 DPI␀pdfgeneralpage|resolution150 DPI␀pdfgeneralpage|resolution300 DPI␀pdfgeneralpage|resolution600 DPI␀pdfgeneralpage|resolution75 DPI␀pdfgeneralpage|selectedsheets_Selection/Selected sheet(s)␀pdfgeneralpage|selection_Selection␀pdfgeneralpage|singlepagesheetsWhole sheet export␀pdfgeneralpage|slidesSlides:␀pdfgeneralpage|tagged_Tagged PDF (add document structure)␀pdfgeneralpage|tagged|tooltip_textIncludes a document's content structure information in a PDF␀pdfgeneralpage|usereferencexobjectUse reference XObjects␀pdfgeneralpage|viewpdf_View PDF after export␀pdfgeneralpage|watermarkSign with _watermark␀pdfgeneralpage|watermarklabelText:␀pdflinkspage|convert_Convert document references to PDF targets␀pdflinkspage|defaultDefault mode␀pdflinkspage|exportExport bookmarks as named destinations␀pdflinkspage|exporturlExport _URLs relative to file system␀pdflinkspage|export|tooltip_textEnable the checkbox to export bookmarks in your document as named destinations in the PDF document.␀pdflinkspage|extended_tip|convertEnable this checkbox to convert the URLs referencing other ODF files to PDF files with the same name. In the referencing URLs the extensions .odt, .odp, .ods, .odg, and .odm are converted to the extension .pdf.␀pdflinkspage|extended_tip|defaultLinks from your PDF document to other documents will be handled as it is specified in your operating system.␀pdflinkspage|extended_tip|exportEnable the checkbox to export bookmarks in your document as named destinations in the PDF document. The destinations correspond to the location of your bookmarks. Use these destinations to create URL links that point to these locations in the PDF document.␀pdflinkspage|extended_tip|exporturlEnable this checkbox to export URLs to other documents as relative URLs in the file system. See "relative hyperlinks" in the Help.␀pdflinkspage|extended_tip|openinternetCross-document links are opened with the Internet browser. The Internet browser must be able to handle the specified file type inside the hyperlink.␀pdflinkspage|extended_tip|openpdfCross-document links are opened with the PDF reader application that currently shows the document. The PDF reader application must be able to handle the specified file type inside the hyperlink.␀pdflinkspage|label1General␀pdflinkspage|label5Cross-document Links␀pdflinkspage|openinternetOpen _with Internet browser␀pdflinkspage|openpdfOpen with PDF reader application␀pdfoptionsdialog|PdfOptionsDialogPDF Options␀pdfoptionsdialog|digitalsignaturesDigital Signatures␀pdfoptionsdialog|generalGeneral␀pdfoptionsdialog|initialviewInitial View␀pdfoptionsdialog|linksLinks␀pdfoptionsdialog|okE_xport␀pdfoptionsdialog|securitySecurity␀pdfoptionsdialog|userinterfaceUser Interface␀pdfsecuritypage|changeany_Any except extracting pages␀pdfsecuritypage|changecomment_Commenting, filling in form fields␀pdfsecuritypage|changeform_Filling in form fields␀pdfsecuritypage|changeinsdel_Inserting, deleting, and rotating pages␀pdfsecuritypage|changenoneNo_t permitted␀pdfsecuritypage|enablea11yEnable text access for acce_ssibility tools␀pdfsecuritypage|enablecopyEna_ble copying of content␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|changeanyAll changes are permitted, except extracting pages.␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|changecommentOnly commenting and filling in form fields is permitted.␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|changeformOnly filling in form fields is permitted.␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|changeinsdelOnly inserting, deleting, and rotating pages is permitted.␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|changenoneNo changes of the content are permitted.␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|enablea11ySelect to enable text access for accessibility tools.␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|enablecopySelect to enable copying of content to the clipboard.␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|printhighThe document can be printed in high resolution.␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|printlowThe document can only be printed in low resolution (150 dpi). Not all PDF readers honor this setting.␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|printnonePrinting the document is not permitted.␀pdfsecuritypage|extended_tip|setpasswordClick to open a dialog where you enter the passwords.␀pdfsecuritypage|label1Printing␀pdfsecuritypage|label11PDF document will be restricted␀pdfsecuritypage|label12No permission password set␀pdfsecuritypage|label13PDF document will be unrestricted␀pdfsecuritypage|label14PDF document will not be restricted due to PDF/A export.␀pdfsecuritypage|label2File Encryption and Permission␀pdfsecuritypage|label3Changes␀pdfsecuritypage|label30PDF document will not be encrypted due to PDF/A export.␀pdfsecuritypage|label4Content␀pdfsecuritypage|label5Open password set␀pdfsecuritypage|label6PDF document will be encrypted␀pdfsecuritypage|label7No open password set␀pdfsecuritypage|label8PDF document will not be encrypted␀pdfsecuritypage|label9Permission password set␀pdfsecuritypage|printhigh_High resolution␀pdfsecuritypage|printlow_Low resolution (150 dpi)␀pdfsecuritypage|printnone_Not permitted␀pdfsecuritypage|setpasswordSet _Passwords…␀pdfsecuritypage|setpasswordstitleSet Passwords␀pdfsignpage|clear_Clear␀pdfsignpage|extended_tip|certAllows you to select a certificate to be used for signing this PDF export.␀pdfsignpage|extended_tip|contactThese three fields allow you to optionally enter additional information about the digital signature that will be applied to the PDF (Where, by whom and why it was made). It will be embedded in the appropriate PDF fields and will be visible to anyone viewing the PDF. Each or all of the three fields may be left blank.␀pdfsignpage|extended_tip|locationThese three fields allow you to optionally enter additional information about the digital signature that will be applied to the PDF (Where, by whom and why it was made). It will be embedded in the appropriate PDF fields and will be visible to anyone viewing the PDF. Each or all of the three fields may be left blank.␀pdfsignpage|extended_tip|passwordEnter the password used for protecting the private key associated with the selected certificate.␀pdfsignpage|extended_tip|reasonThese three fields allow you to optionally enter additional information about the digital signature that will be applied to the PDF (Where, by whom and why it was made). It will be embedded in the appropriate PDF fields and will be visible to anyone viewing the PDF. Each or all of the three fields may be left blank.␀pdfsignpage|extended_tip|selectOpens the Select X.509 Certificate dialog.␀pdfsignpage|label1Certificate␀pdfsignpage|label12Location:␀pdfsignpage|label13Contact information:␀pdfsignpage|label14Reason:␀pdfsignpage|label15Time Stamp Authority:␀pdfsignpage|label2Use this certificate to digitally sign PDF documents:␀pdfsignpage|label7Certificate password:␀pdfsignpage|selectSelect...␀pdfsignpage|tsaNone␀pdfuserinterfacepage|allbookmarksShow _All␀pdfuserinterfacepage|center_Center window on screen␀pdfuserinterfacepage|display_Display document title␀pdfuserinterfacepage|effects_Use transition effects␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|allbookmarksSelect to show all bookmark levels when the reader opens the PDF file.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|centerSelect to generate a PDF file that is shown in a reader window centered on screen.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|displaySelect to generate a PDF file that is shown with the document title in the reader's title bar.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|effectsSelect to export Impress slide transition effects to respective PDF effects.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|menubarSelect to hide the reader's menu bar when the document is active.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|openSelect to generate a PDF file that is shown in a full screen reader window in front of all other windows.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|resizeSelect to generate a PDF file that is shown in a window displaying the whole initial page.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|toolbarSelect to hide the reader's toolbar when the document is active.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|visiblebookmarkSelect to show bookmark levels down to the selected level when the reader opens the PDF file.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|visiblelevelSelect to show bookmark levels down to the selected level when the reader opens the PDF file.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|extended_tip|windowSelect to hide the reader's controls when the document is active.␀pdfuserinterfacepage|label1Window Options␀pdfuserinterfacepage|label2User Interface Options␀pdfuserinterfacepage|label3Transitions␀pdfuserinterfacepage|label4Collapse Outlines␀pdfuserinterfacepage|menubarHide _menubar␀pdfuserinterfacepage|open_Open in full screen mode␀pdfuserinterfacepage|resize_Resize window to initial page␀pdfuserinterfacepage|toolbarHide _toolbar␀pdfuserinterfacepage|visiblebookmark_Visible levels:␀pdfuserinterfacepage|windowHide _window controls␀pdfviewpage|contfacinglayoutCo_ntinuous facing␀pdfviewpage|contlayoutC_ontinuous␀pdfviewpage|defaultlayoutD_efault␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|contfacinglayoutSelect to generate a PDF file that shows pages side by side in a continuous column. For more than two pages, the first page is displayed on the right.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|contlayoutSelect to generate a PDF file that shows pages in a continuous vertical column.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|defaultlayoutSelect to generate a PDF file that shows the pages according to the layout setting of the reader software.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|firstonleftSelect to generate a PDF file that shows pages side by side in a continuous column. For more than two pages, the first page is displayed on the left. You must enable support for complex text layout on Languages and Locales - General in the Options dialog box.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|fitdefaultSelect to generate a PDF file that shows the page contents without zooming. If the reader software is configured to use a zoom factor by default, the page shows with that zoom factor.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|fitvisSelect to generate a PDF file that shows the text and graphics on the page zoomed to fit the reader's window.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|fitwidthSelect to generate a PDF file that shows the page zoomed to fit the width of the reader's window.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|fitwinSelect to generate a PDF file that shows the page zoomed to fit entirely into the reader's window.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|fitzoomSelect a given zoom factor when the reader opens the PDF file.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|outlineSelect to generate a PDF file that shows a bookmarks palette and the page contents.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|pageSelect to show the given page when the reader opens the PDF file.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|pageonlySelect to generate a PDF file that shows only the page contents.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|singlelayoutSelect to generate a PDF file that shows one page at a time.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|thumbsSelect to generate a PDF file that shows a thumbnails palette and the page contents.␀pdfviewpage|extended_tip|zoomSelect a given zoom factor when the reader opens the PDF file.␀pdfviewpage|firstonleftFirst page is _left␀pdfviewpage|fitdefault_Default␀pdfviewpage|fitvisFit _visible␀pdfviewpage|fitwidthFit _width␀pdfviewpage|fitwin_Fit in window␀pdfviewpage|fitzoom_Zoom factor:␀pdfviewpage|label1Page Layout␀pdfviewpage|label2Panes␀pdfviewpage|label3Magnification␀pdfviewpage|label4Open on pa_ge:␀pdfviewpage|outlineOutl_ine and page␀pdfviewpage|pageonly_Page only␀pdfviewpage|singlelayout_Single page␀pdfviewpage|thumbs_Thumbnails and page␀stock_Add␀stock_Apply␀stock_Cancel␀stock_Close␀stock_Delete␀stock_Edit␀stock_Help␀stock_New␀stock_No␀stock_OK␀stock_Remove␀stock_Reset␀stock_Yes␀testxmlfilter|TestXMLFilterDialogTest XML Filter: %s␀testxmlfilter|currentdocumentCurrent Document␀testxmlfilter|displaysourceDisplay source␀testxmlfilter|exportbrowseBrowse...␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|TestXMLFilterDialogTests the XSLT stylesheets used by the selected XML filter.␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|currentdocumentThe front-most open file that matches the XML filter criteria will be used to test the filter. The current XML export filter transforms the file and the resulting XML code is displayed in the XML Filter output window.␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|currentfilenameDisplays the file name of the document that you want to use to test the XSLT filter.␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|displaysourceOpens the XML source of the selected document in your default XML editor after importing.␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|exportbrowseLocate the file that you want to apply the XML export filter to. The XML code of the transformed file is opened in your default XML editor after transformation.␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|exportxsltfileDisplays the file name of the XSLT filter that you entered on the Transformation tab page.␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|importbrowseOpens a file selection dialog. The selected file is opened using the current XML import filter.␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|importxsltfileDisplays the file name of the XSLT filter that you entered on the Transformation tab page.␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|importxslttemplateDisplays the file name of the template that you entered on the Transformation tab page.␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|recentfileRe-opens the document that was last opened with this dialog.␀testxmlfilter|extended_tip|recentfilenameRe-opens the document that was last opened with this dialog.␀testxmlfilter|importbrowseBrowse...␀testxmlfilter|label1Export␀testxmlfilter|label2Import␀testxmlfilter|label3XSLT for export␀testxmlfilter|label4Transform document␀testxmlfilter|label5XSLT for import␀testxmlfilter|label6Transform file␀testxmlfilter|recentfileRecent File␀testxmlfilter|templateimportTemplate for import␀warnpdfdialog|WarnPDFDialogDuring PDF export the following problems occurred:␀warnpdfdialog|WarnPDFDialogProblems During PDF Export␀xmlfiltersettings|XMLFilterSettingsDialogXML Filter Settings␀xmlfiltersettings|delete_Delete...␀xmlfiltersettings|edit_Edit...␀xmlfiltersettings|extended_tip|XMLFilterSettingsDialogOpens the XML Filter Settings dialog, where you can create, edit, delete, and test filters to import and to export XML files.␀xmlfiltersettings|extended_tip|closeCloses the dialog.␀xmlfiltersettings|extended_tip|deleteDeletes the selected file after you confirm the dialog that follows.␀xmlfiltersettings|extended_tip|editOpens a dialog for editing the selected filter.␀xmlfiltersettings|extended_tip|filterlistSelect one or more filters, then click one of the buttons.␀xmlfiltersettings|extended_tip|helpDisplays the help page for this dialog.␀xmlfiltersettings|extended_tip|newOpens a dialog for creating a new filter.␀xmlfiltersettings|extended_tip|openDisplays an Open dialog to open a filter from an XSLT filter package (*.jar).␀xmlfiltersettings|extended_tip|saveDisplays a Save as dialog to save the selected file as an XSLT filter package (*.jar).␀xmlfiltersettings|extended_tip|testOpens a dialog for testing the selected filter.␀xmlfiltersettings|header_nameName␀xmlfiltersettings|header_typeType␀xmlfiltersettings|new_New...␀xmlfiltersettings|open_Open Package...␀xmlfiltersettings|save_Save as Package...␀xmlfiltersettings|test_Test XSLTs...␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|extended_tip|XmlFilterTabPageGeneralEnter or edit general information for an XML filter.␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|extended_tip|applicationSelect the application that you want to use with the filter.␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|extended_tip|descriptionEnter a comment (optional).␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|extended_tip|extensionEnter the file extension to use when you open a file without specifying a filter. The file extension is used to determine which filter to use.␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|extended_tip|filternameEnter the name that you want to display in the list box of the XML Filter Settings dialog.␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|extended_tip|interfacenameEnter the name that you want to display in the File type box in file dialogs.␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|label2_Filter name:␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|label3_Application:␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|label4_Name of file type:␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|label5File _extension:␀xmlfiltertabpagegeneral|label6Comment_s:␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|browseexportBrows_e...␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|browseimportB_rowse...␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|browsetempBrowse...␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|extended_tip|XmlFilterTabPageTransformationEnter or edit file information for an XML filter.␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|extended_tip|browseexportOpens a file selection dialog.␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|extended_tip|browseimportOpens a file selection dialog.␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|extended_tip|browsetempOpens a file selection dialog.␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|extended_tip|docEnter the DOCTYPE of the XML file.␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|extended_tip|tempimportEnter the name of the template that you want to use for importing. In the template, styles are defined to display XML tags.␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|extended_tip|xsltexportIf this is an export filter, enter the file name of the XSLT stylesheet that you want to use for exporting.␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|extended_tip|xsltimportIf this is an import filter, enter the file name of the XSLT stylesheet that you want to use for importing.␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|filtercbThe filter needs XSLT 2.0 processor␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|label2_DocType:␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|label4_XSLT for export:␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|label5XSLT _for import:␀xmlfiltertabpagetransformation|label6Template for _import:␀xsltfilterdialog|XSLTFilterDialogXML Filter: %s␀xsltfilterdialog|extended_tip|XSLTFilterDialogOpens a dialog for creating a new filter.␀xsltfilterdialog|extended_tip|helpDisplays the help page for this dialog.␀xsltfilterdialog|generalGeneral␀xsltfilterdialog|transformationTransformation␀Project-Id-Version: PACKAGE VERSION
