he elements of a formula to the center.␀alignmentdialog|extended_tip|defaultClick here to save your changes as the default settings for new formulas.␀alignmentdialog|extended_tip|leftAligns the selected elements of a formula to the left.␀alignmentdialog|extended_tip|rightAligns the elements of a formula to the right.␀alignmentdialog|label1Horizontal␀alignmentdialog|left_Left␀alignmentdialog|right_Right␀catalogdialog|CatalogDialogSymbols␀catalogdialog|edit_Edit...␀catalogdialog|extended_tip|CatalogDialogOpens the Symbols dialog, in which you can select a symbol to insert in the formula.␀catalogdialog|extended_tip|editClick here to open the Edit Symbols dialog.␀catalogdialog|extended_tip|okSaves all changes and closes dialog.␀catalogdialog|extended_tip|previewDisplays a preview of the current selection.␀catalogdialog|extended_tip|symbolsetAll symbols are organized into symbol sets. Select the desired symbol set from the list box. The corresponding group of symbols appear in the field below.␀catalogdialog|insert_Insert␀catalogdialog|label1_Symbol set:␀catalogdialog|symbolnameUnknown␀extended_tip|SmathSettingsDefines formula settings that will be valid for all documents.␀extended_tip|frameApplies a thin border to the formula area in the printout.␀extended_tip|norightspacesSpecifies that these space wildcards will be removed if they are at the end of a line.␀extended_tip|saveonlyusedsymbolsSaves only those symbols with each formula that are used in that formula.␀extended_tip|sizenormalPrints the formula without adjusting the current font size.␀extended_tip|sizescaledAdjusts the formula to the page format used in the printout.␀extended_tip|smzoomReduces or enlarges the size of the formula code by a specified enlargement factor.␀extended_tip|textSpecifies whether to include the contents of the Commands window at the bottom of the printout.␀extended_tip|titleSpecifies whether you want the name of the document to be included in the printout.␀extended_tip|zoomReduces or enlarges the size of the printed formula by a specified enlargement factor.␀fontdialog|FontDialogFonts␀fontdialog|bold_Bold␀fontdialog|extended_tip|FontDialogUse this dialog to select the font for the respective category in the Fonts dialog.␀fontdialog|extended_tip|boldCheck this box to assign the bold attribute to the font.␀fontdialog|extended_tip|fontSelect a font from the list.␀fontdialog|extended_tip|italicCheck this box to assign the italic attribute to the font.␀fontdialog|formulaLFont␀fontdialog|formulaL1Attributes␀fontdialog|italic_Italic␀fontsizedialog|FontSizeDialogFont Sizes␀fontsizedialog|default_Default␀fontsizedialog|extended_tip|FontSizeDialogUse this dialog to specify the font sizes for your formula. Select a base size and all elements of the formula will be scaled in relation to this base.␀fontsizedialog|extended_tip|defaultClick this button to save your changes as a default for all new formulas.␀fontsizedialog|extended_tip|spinB_baseSizeAll elements of a formula are proportionally scaled to the base size. To change the base size, select or type in the desired point (pt) size. You can also use other units of measure or other metrics, which are then automatically converted to points.␀fontsizedialog|extended_tip|spinB_functionSelect the relative size for names and other function elements in a formula in proportion to the base size.␀fontsizedialog|extended_tip|spinB_indexSelect the relative size for the indexes in a formula in proportion to the base size.␀fontsizedialog|extended_tip|spinB_limitSelect the relative size for the limits in a formula in proportion to the base size.␀fontsizedialog|extended_tip|spinB_operatorSelect the relative size of the mathematical operators in a formula in proportion to the base size.␀fontsizedialog|extended_tip|spinB_textSelect the size for text in a formula relative to the base size.␀fontsizedialog|label1Relative Sizes␀fontsizedialog|label2_Operators:␀fontsizedialog|label3_Limits:␀fontsizedialog|label4Base _size:␀fontsizedialog|label5_Text:␀fontsizedialog|label6_Indexes:␀fontsizedialog|label7_Functions:␀fonttypedialog|FontsDialogFonts␀fonttypedialog|customLCustom Fonts␀fonttypedialog|default_Default␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|FontsDialogDefines the fonts that can be applied to formula elements.␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|defaultClick this button to save your changes as the default for all new formulas.␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|fixedCBYou can specify the font to be used for fixed-width font.␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|functionCBSelect the font for names and properties of functions.␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|mathCBYou can select the font for the math symbols in your formula.␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|modifyClick one of the choices from this pop-up menu to access the Fonts dialog, where you can define the font and attributes for the respective formula and for custom fonts.␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|numberCBYou can select the font for the numbers in your formula.␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|sansCBYou can specify the font to be used for sans serif font.␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|serifCBYou can specify the font to be used as serif font.␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|textCBDefine the font for the text in your formula here.␀fonttypedialog|extended_tip|variableCBYou can select the font for the variables in your formula.␀fonttypedialog|formulaLFormula Fonts␀fonttypedialog|label1_Math:␀fonttypedialog|label1_Variables:␀fonttypedialog|label2_Functions:␀fonttypedialog|label3_Numbers:␀fonttypedialog|label4_Text:␀fonttypedialog|label5_Serif:␀fonttypedialog|label6S_ans-serif:␀fonttypedialog|label7F_ixed-width:␀fonttypedialog|menuitem0_Math␀fonttypedialog|menuitem1_Variables␀fonttypedialog|menuitem2_Functions␀fonttypedialog|menuitem3_Numbers␀fonttypedialog|menuitem4_Text␀fonttypedialog|menuitem5_Serif␀fonttypedialog|menuitem6S_ans-serif␀fonttypedialog|menuitem7Fixe_d-width␀fonttypedialog|modify_Modify␀mathel