ght3Click twice to turn the light source on, and then select a color for the light from the list. If you want, you can also set the color of the surrounding light, by selecting a color from the Ambient light box.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|light4Click twice to turn the light source on, and then select a color for the light from the list. If you want, you can also set the color of the surrounding light, by selecting a color from the Ambient light box.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|light5Click twice to turn the light source on, and then select a color for the light from the list. If you want, you can also set the color of the surrounding light, by selecting a color from the Ambient light box.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|light6Click twice to turn the light source on, and then select a color for the light from the list. If you want, you can also set the color of the surrounding light, by selecting a color from the Ambient light box.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|light7Click twice to turn the light source on, and then select a color for the light from the list. If you want, you can also set the color of the surrounding light, by selecting a color from the Ambient light box.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|light8Click twice to turn the light source on, and then select a color for the light from the list. If you want, you can also set the color of the surrounding light, by selecting a color from the Ambient light box.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|lightcolor1Select a color for the current light source.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|materialChanges the coloring of the selected 3D object.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|modeSelect the shading method that you want to use. Flat shading assigns a single color to a single polygon on the surface of the object. Gouraud shading blends colors across the polygons. Phong shading averages the color of each pixel based on the pixels that surround it, and requires the most processing power.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|objcolorSelect the color that you want to apply to the object.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|objspecificRenders the 3D surface according to the shape of the object. For example, a circular shape is rendered with a spherical surface.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|representationSets the shading and shadow options for the selected 3D object.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|scaleddepthEnter the amount by which to increase or decrease the area of the front side of the selected 3D object.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|shadowAdds or removes a shadow from the selected 3D object.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|slantEnter an angle from 0 to 90 degrees for an imaginary plane on which the shadow is cast.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|speccolorSelect the color that you want the object to reflect.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|sphericalRenders a smooth 3D surface.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|texcirclexWraps the horizontal axis of the texture pattern around a sphere.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|texcircleyWraps the vertical axis of the texture pattern around a sphere.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|texcolorConverts the texture to color.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|texfilterBlurs the texture slightly to remove unwanted speckles.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|texmodulateApplies the texture with shading. To define the shading options for the texture, click the Shading button in this dialog.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|texobjxAutomatically adjusts the texture based on the shape and size of the object.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|texobjyAutomatically adjusts the texture based on the shape and size of the object.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|texparallelxApplies the texture parallel to the horizontal axis.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|texparallelyApplies the texture parallel to the vertical axis.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|texreplaceApplies the texture without shading.␀docking3deffects|extended_tip|textureSets the properties of the surface texture for the selected 3