lors. To modify the current list of colors, deselect the image, choose Format - Area, and then click the Colors tab.␀dockingcolorreplace|extended_tip|color5Select the color to replace the transparent areas in the current image.␀dockingcolorreplace|extended_tip|pipetteSelect one of the four source color boxes. Move the mouse pointer over the selected image, and then click the color that you want to replace.␀dockingcolorreplace|extended_tip|replaceReplaces the selected source colors in the current image with the colors that you specify in the Replace with boxes.␀dockingcolorreplace|extended_tip|tol1Set the tolerance for replacing a source color in the source image. To replace colors that are similar to the color that you selected, enter a low value. To replace a wider range of colors, enter a higher value.␀dockingcolorreplace|extended_tip|tol2Set the tolerance for replacing a source color in the source image. To replace colors that are similar to the color that you selected, enter a low value. To replace a wider range of colors, enter a higher value.␀dockingcolorreplace|extended_tip|tol3Set the tolerance for replacing a source color in the source image. To replace colors that are similar to the color that you selected, enter a low value. To replace a wider range of colors, enter a higher value.␀dockingcolorreplace|extended_tip|tol4Set the tolerance for replacing a source color in the source image. To replace colors that are similar to the color that you selected, enter a low value. To replace a wider range of colors, enter a higher value.␀dockingcolorreplace|extended_tip|toolgridDisplays the color in the selected image that directly underlies the current mouse pointer position. This features only works if the Color Replacer tool is selected.␀dockingcolorreplace|label1Colors␀dockingcolorreplace|label2Source color␀dockingcolorreplace|label3Tolerance␀dockingcolorreplace|label4Replace with...␀dockingcolorreplace|pipettePipette␀dockingcolorreplace|replace_Replace␀dockingcolorreplace|tol1-atkobjectTolerance 1␀dockingcolorreplace|tol2-atkobjectTolerance 2␀dockingcolorreplace|tol3-atkobjectTolerance 3␀dockingcolorreplace|tol4-atkobjectTolerance 4␀dockingfontwork|autosize|tooltip_textAutoSize Text␀dockingfontwork|center|tooltip_textAlign Center␀dockingfontwork|color|tooltip_textShadow Color␀dockingfontwork|contour|tooltip_textContour␀dockingfontwork|distancex|tooltip_textDistance X␀dockingfontwork|distancey|tooltip_textDistance Y␀dockingfontwork|distance|tooltip_textDistance␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|DockingFontworkSimple tool for putting text along a curve without any fancy effects.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|autosizeResizes the text to fit the length of the text baseline.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|centerCenters the text on the text baseline.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|colorSelect a color for the text shadow.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|contourShows or hides the text baseline, or the edges of the selected object.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|distanceEnter the amount of space that you want to leave between the text baseline and the base of the individual characters.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|distancexEnter the horizontal distance between the text characters and the edge of the shadow or the angle of the shadow slant from vertical.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|distanceyEnter the vertical distance between the text characters and the edge of the shadow, or the size of the shadow in percent values of the character size.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|horiHorizontally slants the characters in the text object.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|indentEnter the amount of space to leave between the beginning of the text baseline, and the beginning of the text.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|leftAligns the text to the left end of the text baseline.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|noshadowRemoves the shadow effects that you applied to the text.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|offRemoves baseline formatting.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|orientationReverses the text flow direction, and flips the text horizontally or vertically. To use this command, you must first apply a different baseline to the text.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|rightAligns the text to the right end of the text baseline.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|rotateUses the top or the bottom edge of the selected object as the text baseline.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|slantAdds a slant shadow to the text in the selected object. Click this button, and then enter the dimensions of the shadow in the Distance X and the Distance Y boxes.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|textcontourShows or hides the borders of the individual characters in the text.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|uprightUses the top or the bottom edge of the selected object as the text baseline and preserves the original vertical alignment of the individual characters.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|vertVertically slants the characters in the text object.␀dockingfontwork|extended_tip|verticalAdds a shadow to the text in the selected object. Click this button, and then enter the dimensions of the shadow in the Distance X and the Distance Y boxes.␀dockingfontwork|hori|tooltip_textSlant Horizontal␀dockingfontwork|indent|tooltip_textIndent␀dockingfontwork|left|tooltip_textAlign Left␀dockingfontwork|noshadow|tooltip_textNo Text Shadow␀dockingfontwork|off|tooltip_textBaseline Off␀dockingfontwork|orientation|tooltip_textOrientation␀dockingfontwork|right|tooltip_textAlign Right␀dockingfontwork|rotate|tooltip_textRotate␀dockingfontwork|slant|tooltip_textSlant Text Shadow␀dockingfontwork|textcontour|tooltip_textText Contour␀dockingfontwork|upright|tooltip_textUpright␀dockingfontwork|vertical|tooltip_textAdd Text Shadow␀dockingfontwork|vert|tooltip_textSlant Vertical␀dockingwindow|RID_SVXSTR_PARALLELP_arallel␀docrecoverybrokendialog|DocRecoveryBrokenDialog%PRODUCTNAME Document Recovery␀docrecoverybrokendialog|changeChan_ge...␀docrecoverybrokendialog|label1The automatic recovery process was interrupted.

The documents listed below will be saved in the folder noted below if you click 'Save'. Click 'Cancel' to close the wizard without saving the documents.␀docrecoverybrokendialog|label3Documents:␀docrecoverybrokendialog|label4_Save to:␀docrecoverybrokendialog|save_Save␀docrecoveryprogressdialog|DocRecoveryProgressDialogDocuments Are Being Saved␀docrecoveryprogressdialog|label2Progress of saving:␀docrecoveryrecoverdialog|DocRecoveryRecoverDialog%PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION Document Recovery␀docrecoveryrecoverdialog|cancel_Discard All␀docrecoveryrecoverdialog|desc%PRODUCTNAME will attempt to recover the state of the files you were working on before it crashed. Click 'Recover Selected' to begin the process, or click 'Discard' to cancel the recovery.␀docrecoveryrecoverdialog|label2Status of recovered documents:␀docrecoveryrecoverdialog|next_Recover Selected␀docrecoveryrecoverdialog|recoverftRecover Document␀docrecoveryrecoverdialog|statusftStatus␀docrecoverysavedialog|DocRecoverySaveDialog%PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION Document Recovery␀docrecoverysavedialog|label1Due to an error, %PRODUCTNAME crashed. All the files you were working on will now be saved. The next time %PRODUCTNAME is launched, your files will be recovered automatically.␀docrecoverysavedialog|label2The following files will be recovered:␀extended_tip|OptGridPageSpecifies the settings for the configurable grid on your document pages. This grid helps you determine the exact position of your objects. You can also set this grid in line with the "magnetic" snap grid.␀extended_tip|bigorthoSpecifies that a square is created based on the longer side of a rectangle when the Shift key is pressed before you release the mouse button. This also applies to an ellipse (a circle will be created based on the longest diameter of the ellipse). When the Extend edges box is not marked, a square or a circle will be created based on the shorter side or diameter.␀extended_tip|gridvisibleSpecifies whether to display the grid.␀extended_tip|mtrfldangleSpecifies that graphic objects can only be rotated within the rotation angle that you selected in the When rotating control.␀extended_tip|mtrfldbezangleDefines the angle for point reduction.␀extended_tip|mtrflddrawxDefines the unit of measure for the spacing between grid points on the X-axis.␀extended_tip|mtrflddrawyDefines the grid points spacing in the currently selected unit of measurement on the Y-axis.␀extended_tip|mtrfldsnapareaDefines the snap distance between the mouse pointer and the object contour. Impress snaps to a snap point if the mouse pointer is nearer than the distance selected in the Snap range control.␀extended_tip|numflddivisionxSpecify the number of intermediate spaces between grid points on the X-axis.␀extended_tip|numflddivisionySpecify the number of intermediate spaces between grid points on the Y-axis.␀extended_tip|orthoSpecifies that graphic objects are restricted vertically, horizontally or diagonally (45°) when creating or moving them.␀extended_tip|rotateSpecifies that graphic objects can only be rotated within the rotation angle that you selected in the When rotating control.␀extended_tip|snapborderSpecifies whether to align the contour of the graphic object to the nearest page margin.␀extended_tip|snapframeSpecifies whether to align the contour of the graphic object to the border of the nearest graphic object.␀extended_tip|snaphelplinesSnaps the edge of a dragged object to the nearest snap line when you release the mouse.␀extended_tip|snappointsSpecifies whether to align the contour of the graphic object to the points of the nearest graphic object.␀extended_tip|synchronizeSpecifies whether to change the current grid settings symmetrically.␀extended_tip|usegridsnapSpecifies whether to move frames, drawing elements, and controls only between grid points.␀extrustiondepthdialog|ExtrustionDepthDialogExtrusion Depth␀extrustiondepthdialog|extended_tip|ExtrustionDepthDialogEnter an extrusion d