IVEActive␀imapdialog|TBI_APPLYApply␀imapdialog|TBI_CIRCLEEllipse␀imapdialog|TBI_CLOSEClose␀imapdialog|TBI_FREEPOLYFreeform Polygon␀imapdialog|TBI_MACROMacro...␀imapdialog|TBI_OPENOpen...␀imapdialog|TBI_POLYPolygon␀imapdialog|TBI_POLYDELETEDelete Points␀imapdialog|TBI_POLYEDITEdit Points␀imapdialog|TBI_POLYINSERTInsert Points␀imapdialog|TBI_POLYMOVEMove Points␀imapdialog|TBI_PROPERTYProperties...␀imapdialog|TBI_RECTRectangle␀imapdialog|TBI_REDORedo␀imapdialog|TBI_SAVEASSave...␀imapdialog|TBI_SELECTSelect␀imapdialog|TBI_UNDOUndo ␀imapdialog|extended_tip|ImapDialogAllows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a graphic or a group of graphics. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.␀imapdialog|extended_tip|TBI_ACTIVEDisables or enables the hyperlink for the selected hotspot. A disabled hotspot is transparent.␀imapdialog|extended_tip|TBI_APPLYApplies the changes that you made to the image map.␀imapdialog|extended_tip|TBI_CIRCLEDraws an elliptical hotspot where you drag in the graphic. After, you can enter the Address and the Text for the hotspot, and then select the Frame where you want the URL to open.␀imapdialog|extended_tip|TBI_FREEPOLYDraws a hotspot that is based on a freeform polygon. Click this icon and move to where you want to draw the hotspot. Drag a freeform line and release to close the shape. After, you can enter the Address and the Text for the hotspot, and then select the Frame where you want the URL to open.␀imapdialog|extended_tip|TBI_MACROLets you assign a macro that runs when you click the selected hotspot in a browser.␀imapdialog|extended_tip|TBI_OPENLoads an existing image map in the MAP-CERN, MAP-NCSA or SIP StarView ImageMap file format.␀imapdialog|extended_tip|TBI_POLYDraws a polygonal hotspot in the graphic. Click this icon, drag in the graphic, and then click to define one side of the polygon. Move to where you want to place the end of the next side, and then click. Repeat until you have draw