Use the browse button to select a database file.␀extended tip | companyType the name of your company in this field.␀extended tip | emailType your company email address.␀extended tip | emailType your email address.␀extended tip | faxType company fax number in this field.␀extended tip | faxType your fax number in this field.␀extended tip | firstnameType your first name.␀extended tip | icityType the city where you live.␀extended tip | icityType the company city␀extended tip | izipType company ZIP in this field.␀extended tip | izipType your ZIP in this field.␀extended tip | lastnameType your last name.␀extended tip | positionType your position in the company in this field.␀extended tip | shortnameType your initials.␀extended tip | stateType company state.␀extended tip | stateType your state.␀extended tip | streetType the name of company street in this field.␀extended tip | streetType the name of your street in this field.␀extended tip | titleType your title in this field.␀extended tips | company2Company second line␀extended tips | countryCompany country␀extended tips | countryType the country name␀extended tips | firstname2Type your first name␀extended tips | jobType your profession␀extended tips | lastname2Type your last name ␀extended tips | mobileType company mobile␀extended tips | mobileType your mobile phone number␀extended tips | phoneType business phone␀extended tips | phoneType your phone number␀extended tips | shortname2Type your initials␀extended tips | sloganCompany slogan␀extended tips | urlCompany homepage␀extended tips | urlEnter your home page␀extended_tip|MailConfigPageSpecifies the user information and server settings for when you send form letters as email messages.␀extended_tip|OptCaptionPageSelect the object type for which the AutoCaption settings are to be valid.␀extended_tip|OptCompatPageSpecifies compatibility settings for text documents. These options help in fine-tuning Writer when importing Microsoft Word documents.␀extended_tip|OptFontTabPageSpecifies the settings for the basic fonts in your documents.␀extended_tip|OptFormatAidsPageIn Writer text and HTML documents, defines the display for certain characters and for the direct cursor.␀extended_tip|OptGeneralPageSpecifies general settings for text documents.␀extended_tip|OptRedLinePageDefines the appearance of changes in the document.␀extended_tip|OptTablePageDefines the attributes of tables in text documents.␀extended_tip|PrintOptionsPageSpecifies print settings within a text or HTML document.␀extended_tip|ViewOptionsPageDefines the default settings for displaying objects in your text documents and also the default settings for the window elements.␀extended_tip|addressEnter your email address for replies.␀extended_tip|alwaysAlways updates links while loading a document, and only if the document is in a trusted file location or the global security level is Low (Not recommended).␀extended_tip|authenticationEnables the authentication that is required to send email by SMTP.␀extended_tip|blankpagesIf this option is enabled, automatically-inserted blank pages are being printed. This is best if you are printing double-sided. For example, in a book, a "chapter" paragraph style has been set to always start with an odd numbered page. If the previous chapter ends on an odd page, Writer inserts an even numbered blank page. This option controls whether to print that even numbered page or not.␀extended_tip|borderSpecifies that table cells have a border by default.␀extended_tip|breakDisplays all line breaks inserted with the Shift+Enter shortcut. These breaks create a new line, but do not start a new paragraph.␀extended_tip|brochureSelect the Brochure option to print your document in brochure format.␀extended_tip|categorySpecifies the category of the selected object.␀extended_tip|changedDefines how changes to text attributes are displayed in the document. These changes affect attributes such as bold, italic or underline.␀extended_tip|changedcolorYou can also choose a color to display each type of recorded change. When you choose the condition "By author" in the list, the color is automatically determined by Writer, then modified to match to the author of each change.␀extended_tip|changesinmarginDisplays text that is hidden by Conditional Text or Hidden Text fields.␀extended_tip|colinsertSpecifies the default value for inserting columns.␀extended_tip|colmoveSpecifies the step size value when moving a column with the keyboard.␀extended_tip|commentsDisplays comments. Click a comment to edit the text. Use the context menu in Navigator to locate or delete a comment. Use the comments's context menu to delete this comment or all comments or all comments of this author.␀extended_tip|cursorinprotSpecifies that you can set the cursor in a protected area, but cannot make any changes.␀extended_tip|cursoronoffActivates the direct cursor.␀extended_tip|defaultClick to use the current settings on this tab page as the default for further sessions with Writer.␀extended_tip|deletedSpecifies how changes in the document are displayed when text is deleted. If you record text deletions, the text is displayed with the selected attribute (for example, strikethrough) and is not deleted.␀extended_tip|deletedcolorYou can also choose a color to display each type of recorded change. When you choose the condition "By author" in the list, the color is automatically determined by Writer, then modified to match to the author of each change.␀extended_tip|displaynameEnter your name.␀extended_tip|dontsplitSpecifies that tables are not split by any type of text flow break.␀extended_tip|drawingsDisplays the drawings and controls contained in your document.␀extended_tip|endpagePrint comments on a new page after the current page.␀extended_tip|errorsIn the Errors list box you can read an explanation of any errors encountered while testing the settings.␀extended_tip|faxIf you have installed fax software on your computer and wish to fax directly from the text document, select the desired fax machine.␀extended_tip|fixSpecifies that changes to a row or column only affect the corresponding adjacent area.␀extended_tip|fixpropSpecifies that changes to a row or column have an effect on the entire table.␀extended_tip|formcontrolsSpecifies whether the form control fields of the text document are printed.␀extended_tip|graphicsSpecifies whether the graphics of your text document are printed.␀extended_tip|graphicsSpecifies whether to display images and objects on the screen.␀extended_tip|headerSpecifies that the first row of the table is formatted with the "Table heading" Paragraph Style.␀extended_tip|helplinesDisplays snap lines around the frames when frames are moved. You can select the Helplines While Moving option to show the exact position of the object using lineal values.␀extended_tip|hiddenparafieldIf you have inserted text using the Hidden Paragraph field, specifies whether to display the hidden paragraph.␀extended_tip|hiddentextDisplays text that uses the character format "hidden", when View - Formatting Marks is enabled.␀extended_tip|hiddentextEnable this option to print text that is marked as hidden.␀extended_tip|hiddentextfieldDisplays text that is hidden by Conditional Text or Hidden Text fields.␀extended_tip|hrulerDisplays the horizontal ruler. Select the desired measurement unit from the corresponding list.␀extended_tip|hrulercomboboxDisplays the horizontal ruler. Select the desired measurement unit from the corresponding list.␀extended_tip|hyphensSpecifies whether soft hyphens (called also as optional or discretionary hyphens) are displayed. These are hidden user-defined delimiters that you enter within a word by pressing Ctrl+Hyphen(-). Words with soft hyphens are only separated at the end of a line at the point where a soft hyphen has been inserted, irrespective of whether the automatic hyphenation is activated or deactivated.␀extended_tip|idxboxSpecifies the font used for indexes, alphabetical indexes, and tables of contents.␀extended_tip|imapSpecifies that the incoming mail server uses IMAP.␀extended_tip|inblackSpecifies whether to always print text in black.␀extended_tip|indexheightSpecifies the size of the font.␀extended_tip|inpasswordEnter the password.␀extended_tip|insertSpecifies how changes in the document are displayed when text is inserted.␀extended_tip|insertcolorYou can also choose a color to display each type of recorded change. When you choose the condition "By author" in the list, the color is automatically determined by Writer, then modified to match to the author of each change.␀extended_tip|inusernameEnter the user name for the IMAP server.␀extended_tip|label5If you have installed fax software on your computer and wish to fax directly from the text document, select the desired fax machine.␀extended_tip|labelboxSpecifies the font used for the captions of images and tables.␀extended_tip|labelheightSpecifies the size of the font.␀extended_tip|leftpagesSpecifies whether to print all left (even numbered) pages of the document.␀extended_tip|listboxSpecifies the fonts for lists and numbering and all derived styles.␀extended_tip|listheightSpecifies the size of the font.␀extended_tip|markcolorSpecifies the color for highlighting the changed lines in the text.␀extended_tip|markposDefines if and where changed lines in the document are marked.␀extended_tip|measureunitSpecifies the Unit for HTML documents.␀extended_tip|metricSpecifies the unit of measurement for text documents.␀extended_tip|neverLinks are never updated while loading a document.␀extended_tip|nonbreakSpecifies that non-breaking spaces are shown as gray boxes. Non-breaking spaces are not broken at the end of a line and are entered with the Ctrl+Shift+Spacebar shortcut keys.␀extended_tip|numalignmentSpecifies that numbers are always bottom right aligned in the cell.␀extended_tip|numfmtformattingIf Number format recognition is not marked, only input in the format that has been set at the cell is accepted. Any other input resets the format to Text.␀extended_tip|numformattingSpecifies that numbers in a text table are recognized and formatted as numbers.␀extended_tip|objectsSelect the object type for which the AutoCaption settings are to be valid.␀extended_tip|onrequestUpdates links only on request while loading a document.␀extended_tip|outpasswordEnter the password for the user name.␀extended_tip|papertrayFor printers with multiple trays, the "Paper tray from printer settings" option specifies whether the paper tray used is specified by the system settings of the printer.␀extended_tip|paragraphSpecifies whether paragraph delimiters are displayed. The paragraph delimiters also contain paragraph format information.␀extended_tip|pop3Specifies that the incoming mail server uses POP 3.␀extended_tip|portEnter the SMTP port.␀extended_tip|portEnter the port on the POP3 or IMAP server.␀extended_tip|repeatheaderSpecifies whether the table heading is carried over onto the new page after a page break.␀extended_tip|replytoEnter the address to use for email replies.␀extended_tip|replytocbUses the email address that you enter in the Reply address text box as the reply-to email address.␀extended_tip|rightpagesSpecifies whether to print all right (odd numbered) pages of the document.␀extended_tip|rowinsertSpecifies the default value for inserting rows.␀extended_tip|rowmoveSpecifies the step size value when moving a row with the keyboard.␀extended_tip|rtlCheck to print the pages of the brochure in the correct order for a right-to-left script.␀extended_tip|secureWhen available, uses a secure connection to send emails.␀extended_tip|separateauthenticationSelect if your SMTP server requires a user name and password.␀extended_tip|serverEnter the SMTP server name.␀extended_tip|serverEnter the server name of your POP 3 or IMAP mail server.␀extended_tip|serverauthenticationOpens the Server Authentication dialog where you can specify the server authentication settings for secure email.␀extended_tip|smoothscrollActivates the smooth page scrolling function. ␀extended_tip|smtpafterpopSelect if you are required to first read your email before you can send email.␀extended_tip|spacesSpecifies whether to represent every space in the text with a dot.␀extended_tip|squaremodeWhen this setting is enabled, the text grid will look like square page.␀extended_tip|standardboxSpecifies the font to be used for the Default Paragraph Style.␀extended_tip|standardheightSpecifies the size of the font.␀extended_tip|stopClick the Stop button to stop a test session manually.␀extended_tip|tabSpecifies the spacing between the individual tab stops.␀extended_tip|tablesDisplays the tables contained in your document.␀extended_tip|tabsSpecifies that tab stops are displayed as small arrows.␀extended_tip|testOpens the Test Account Settings dialog to test the current settings.␀extended_tip|textplaceholderEnable this option to print text placeholders. Disable this option to leave the text placeholders blank in the printout.␀extended_tip|titleboxSpecifies the font to be used for headings.␀extended_tip|titleheightSpecifies the size of the font.␀extended_tip|updatechartsSpecifies whether to automatically update charts. Whenever a Writer table cell value changes and the cursor leaves that cell, the chart that displays the cell value is updated automatically.␀extended_tip|updatefieldsThe contents of all fields are updated automatically whenever the screen contents are displayed as new. Even with this box unchecked, some fields are updated each time a special condition takes place.␀extended_tip|usecharunitWhen this setting is enabled, the measurement units of indents and spacing on Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing tab will be character (ch) and line.␀extended_tip|usernameEnter the user name for the SMTP server.␀extended_tip|varSpecifies that changes to a row or colu