mns.␀printdialog|extended_tip|pageeditEnter the number of page to be shown in the preview.␀printdialog|extended_tip|pagemarginsbSelect margin between individual pages on each sheet of paper.␀printdialog|extended_tip|pageorientationboxSelect the orientation of the paper.␀printdialog|extended_tip|pagerangeTo print a range of pages, use a format like 3-6. To print single pages, use a format like 7;9;11. You can print a combination of page ranges and single pages, by using a format like 3-6;8;10;12.␀printdialog|extended_tip|pagerowsSelect number of rows.␀printdialog|extended_tip|pagespersheetboxSelect how many pages to print per sheet of paper.␀printdialog|extended_tip|pagespersheetbtnPrint multiple pages per sheet of paper.␀printdialog|extended_tip|papersizeboxSet the paper size you would like to use. The preview will show how the document would look on a paper of the given size.␀printdialog|extended_tip|previewThe preview shows how each sheet of paper will look. You can browse through all sheets of paper with the buttons below the preview.␀printdialog|extended_tip|previewboxTurn on or off display of the print preview.␀printdialog|extended_tip|printersboxThe list box shows the installed printers. Click the printer to use for the current print job. Click the Properties button to change some of the printer properties.␀printdialog|extended_tip|rbAllPagesPrints the entire document.␀printdialog|extended_tip|rbRangePagesPrints only the pages or slides that you specify in the Pages box.␀printdialog|extended_tip|rbRangeSelectionPrints only the selected area(s) or object(s) in the current document.␀printdialog|extended_tip|reverseorderCheck to print pages in reverse order.␀printdialog|extended_tip|setupOpens the Printer Properties dialog. The printer properties vary according to the printer that you select.␀printdialog|extended_tip|sheetmarginsbSelect margin between the printed pages and paper edge.␀printdialog|extended_tip|sidesboxIf the printer is capable of